window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b028-d77a95868d85f3e2.json"]={sha256:"d77a95868d85f3e23de5a352524c438e6966bcadca28ea9ebffba9ccf22c685f",value:{"id":"b028","title":"威利斯大樓","titleEn":"Willis Tower","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"威利斯大樓（原希爾斯大樓）由 Fazlur Khan 與 SOM 設計，九個 75 ft（22.9 m）見方的鋼框管組成 225 ft 見方的束筒，管筒在 50、66、90 層分批終止，只留兩管到頂。本課從束筒如何以內部框架減少剪力遲滯、分段收進如何降低質心與造成扭轉，到 15 ft 柱距框管、75 ft 複合樓板桁架、每週兩層的鋼構安裝與岩盤沉箱，再到週期量測、外牆熱隔離，以及 2017–2020 年在營運中改造底座時的柱補強與傳力路徑管理。","summaryEn":"Willis Tower, formerly Sears Tower, designed by Fazlur Khan and SOM, bundles nine 75 ft (22.9 m) square steel framed tubes into a 225 ft square plan; the tubes stop in groups at floors 50, 66 and 90, leaving two to the top. The course covers how interior frames reduce shear lag, how staged terminations lower the mass centroid and create torsion, the 15 ft column module, 75 ft composite floor trusses, erection at two floors a week and rock caissons, then period measurement, thermal isolation by the skin, and column strengthening and load-path control during the 2017–2020 base repositioning of the occupied tower.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-supertall","subcategoryTitle":"超高層建築巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"Supertall building landmarks","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-supertall","learningTags":["structures","st-supertall","tower"],"architectureFamily":"tower","architectureNodes":[["九個 22.9 m 鋼框管","Nine 22.9 m steel framed tubes"],["內部框架腹板","Interior web frames"],["50／66／90 層分段收進","Setbacks at floors 50, 66, 90"],["75 ft 複合樓板桁架","75 ft composite floor trusses"],["岩盤嵌入沉箱","Rock-socketed caissons"],["改造轉換柱與補強","Renovation transfers and strengthening"]],"architectureEdges":[[1,0],[2,0],[3,0],[0,4],[5,0],[5,4]],"diagram":{"type":"tower","labels":["九個 22.9 m 鋼框管","內部框架腹板","50／66／90 層分段收進","75 ft 複合樓板桁架","岩盤嵌入沉箱"],"labelsEn":["Nine 22.9 m steel framed tubes","Interior web frames","Setbacks at floors 50, 66, 90","75 ft composite floor trusses","Rock-socketed caissons"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：以平截面假設估算束筒翼板柱在風傾覆力矩下的軸力。取均布風荷載 w = 1.4 kPa×68.6 m ≈ 96.0 kN/m、高度 H = 442 m，基座力矩 M = wH²/2 = 96.0×442²/2 ≈ 9.38×10⁶ kN·m。抵抗彎矩的翼板線位於 y = ±34.29 m（外牆）與 y = ±11.43 m（內部框架），每線 16 根同斷面柱，Σy² = 16×(2×34.29² + 2×11.43²) ≈ 41,806 m²。角柱軸力 F = M·y/Σy² = 9.38×10⁶×34.29/41,806 ≈ 7,690 kN，內部框架柱約 2,560 kN。若沒有內部框架（單一大管），Σy² = 16×2×34.29² ≈ 37,626 m²，角柱軸力升到約 8,550 kN，增加約 11%；而且單管的剪力遲滯會讓角柱實際軸力再高出更多。若風荷載提高 20%，所有軸力同比例增加。數值為教學假設，忽略腹板柱、剪力遲滯與收進，不代表實際設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: estimate flange-column axial forces in the bundled tube under wind overturning using plane sections. Take a uniform wind load w = 1.4 kPa×68.6 m ≈ 96.0 kN/m and height H = 442 m, so the base moment M = wH²/2 = 96.0×442²/2 ≈ 9.38×10⁶ kN·m. The flange lines resisting the moment lie at y = ±34.29 m (exterior walls) and y = ±11.43 m (interior frames), each with 16 identical columns, so Σy² = 16×(2×34.29² + 2×11.43²) ≈ 41,806 m². The corner-column force is F = M·y/Σy² = 9.38×10⁶×34.29/41,806 ≈ 7,690 kN, and an interior-frame column carries about 2,560 kN. Without interior frames (one large tube), Σy² = 16×2×34.29² ≈ 37,626 m² and the corner force rises to about 8,550 kN, about 11% more, and shear lag in a single tube would push the real corner force higher still. A 20% increase in wind load raises every axial force by the same proportion. Values are teaching assumptions ignoring web columns, shear lag and setbacks, not the actual design.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b028-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「束筒與剪力遲滯」與「管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bundled tubes and shear lag\" and \"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b028-v13-01","title":"束筒與剪力遲滯：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Bundled tubes and shear lag: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「九管束筒與內部腹板」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Nine bundled tubes and interior webs” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"框管結構把密排的周邊柱與深裙梁組成一個空心箱形懸臂，平行風向的兩面像箱梁腹板承受剪力，垂直風向的兩面像翼板承受拉壓。單一大管的翼板中段柱因裙梁剪力變形而「跟不上」角柱，軸力向角落集中，這就是剪力遲滯。束筒在 225 ft 見方的平面中多加兩道縱橫向內部框架，把翼板分成三段、腹板由兩道增為四道，使軸力分布更均勻，剪力勁度也加倍。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「九管束筒與內部腹板」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A framed tube turns closely spaced perimeter columns and deep spandrels into a hollow box cantilever: the two faces parallel to the wind act like the webs of a box girder and carry shear, while the two faces normal to it act like flanges in tension and compression. In a single large tube the flange columns near mid-face lag behind the corners because the spandrels deform in shear, concentrating axial force at the corners; this is shear lag. The bundled tube adds two interior frames in each direction within the 225 ft square, splitting each flange into three segments and doubling the web frames from two to four, which evens out axial forces and doubles shear stiffness. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Nine bundled tubes and interior webs” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：懸臂剪力變形 Δ_s = wH²/(2nK)，n 為腹板框架數、K 為每道框架的等效剪力勁度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Cantilever shear deflection is Δ_s = wH²/(2nK), with n web frames each of equivalent shear stiffness K.","failure":"常見誤解：「框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「九管束筒與內部腹板」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Nine bundled tubes and interior webs”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-01-k1","title":"束筒與剪力遲滯","titleEn":"Bundled tubes and shear lag","text":"框管結構把密排的周邊柱與深裙梁組成一個空心箱形懸臂，平行風向的兩面像箱梁腹板承受剪力，垂直風向的兩面像翼板承受拉壓。單一大管的翼板中段柱因裙梁剪力變形而「跟不上」角柱，軸力向角落集中，這就是剪力遲滯。","textEn":"A framed tube turns closely spaced perimeter columns and deep spandrels into a hollow box cantilever: the two faces parallel to the wind act like the webs of a box girder and carry shear, while the two faces normal to it act like flanges in tension and compression. In a single large tube the flange columns near mid-face lag behind the corners because the spandrels deform in shear, concentrating axial force at the corners; this is shear lag.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「束筒與剪力遲滯」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bundled tubes and shear lag\" is correct?","options":["框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。","框管結構把密排的周邊柱與深裙梁組成一個空心箱形懸臂，平行風向的兩面像箱梁腹板承受剪力，垂直風向的兩面像翼板承受拉壓。","收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally.","A framed tube turns closely spaced perimeter columns and deep spandrels into a hollow box cantilever: the two faces parallel to the wind act like the webs of a box girder and carry shear, while the two faces normal to it act like flanges in tension and compression.","Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"框管結構把密排的周邊柱與深裙梁組成一個空心箱形懸臂，平行風向的兩面像箱梁腹板承受剪力，垂直風向的兩面像翼板承受拉壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A framed tube turns closely spaced perimeter columns and deep spandrels into a hollow box cantilever: the two faces parallel to the wind act like the webs of a box girder and carry shear, while the two faces normal to it act like flanges in tension and compression. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b028-v13-02","title":"束筒與剪力遲滯：定量估算","titleEn":"Bundled tubes and shear lag: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「九管束筒與內部腹板」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Nine bundled tubes and interior webs” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：懸臂剪力變形 Δ_s = wH²/(2nK)，n 為腹板框架數、K 為每道框架的等效剪力勁度。取 w = 1.4 kPa×68.6 m ≈ 96.0 kN/m、H = 442 m、K = 1.0×10⁷ kN：n = 2 時 Δ_s = 96.0×442²/(2×2×10⁷) ≈ 0.469 m；n = 4 時 Δ_s ≈ 0.235 m，減半。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Cantilever shear deflection is Δ_s = wH²/(2nK), with n web frames each of equivalent shear stiffness K. With w = 1.4 kPa×68.6 m ≈ 96.0 kN/m, H = 442 m and K = 1.0×10⁷ kN, n = 2 gives Δ_s = 96.0×442²/(2×2×10⁷) ≈ 0.469 m and n = 4 gives Δ_s ≈ 0.235 m, half as much. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在三維框架模型中比較單一大管與九管束筒在同一風荷載下的翼板柱軸力分布，計算角柱與中段柱的軸力比作為剪力遲滯指標，並把剪力與彎曲兩部分的頂部變位拆開檢討。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In a three-dimensional frame model compare flange-column axial forces for one large tube and for the nine-tube bundle under the same wind load, use the ratio of corner to mid-face column force as a shear-lag index, and separate the shear and bending components of top drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"懸臂剪力變形 Δ_s = wH²/(2nK)，n 為腹板框架數、K 為每道框架的等效剪力勁度。取 w = 1.4 kPa×68.6 m ≈ 96.0 kN/m、H = 442 m、K = 1.0×10⁷ kN：n = 2 時 Δ_s = 96.0×442²/(2×2×10⁷) ≈ 0.469 m；n = 4 時 Δ_s ≈ 0.235 m，減半。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Cantilever shear deflection is Δ_s = wH²/(2nK), with n web frames each of equivalent shear stiffness K. With w = 1.4 kPa×68.6 m ≈ 96.0 kN/m, H = 442 m and K = 1.0×10⁷ kN, n = 2 gives Δ_s = 96.0×442²/(2×2×10⁷) ≈ 0.469 m and n = 4 gives Δ_s ≈ 0.235 m, half as much. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「束筒與剪力遲滯」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bundled tubes and shear lag\", which statement holds?","options":["樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。","沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。","懸臂剪力變形 Δ_s = wH²/(2nK)，n 為腹板框架數、K 為每道框架的等效剪力勁度。"],"optionsEn":["If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour.","A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.","Cantilever shear deflection is Δ_s = wH²/(2nK), with n web frames each of equivalent shear stiffness K."],"answer":2,"explanation":"懸臂剪力變形 Δ_s = wH²/(2nK)，n 為腹板框架數、K 為每道框架的等效剪力勁度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Cantilever shear deflection is Δ_s = wH²/(2nK), with n web frames each of equivalent shear stiffness K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b028-v13-03","title":"束筒與剪力遲滯：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bundled tubes and shear lag: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「九管束筒與內部腹板」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Nine bundled tubes and interior webs” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在三維框架模型中比較單一大管與九管束筒在同一風荷載下的翼板柱軸力分布，計算角柱與中段柱的軸力比作為剪力遲滯指標，並把剪力與彎曲兩部分的頂部變位拆開檢討。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In a three-dimensional frame model compare flange-column axial forces for one large tube and for the nine-tube bundle under the same wind load, use the ratio of corner to mid-face column force as a shear-lag index, and separate the shear and bending components of top drift. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：檢核框管時要以完整三維模型而非平面等效梁取得角柱設計力，並把角柱、角隅接頭與內部框架交會柱列為加強檢驗的構件類別。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check framed tubes with a full three-dimensional model rather than an equivalent plane beam to obtain corner-column design forces, and place corner columns, corner joints and columns where interior frames intersect in an enhanced inspection category.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略剪力遲滯會低估角柱與其接頭的軸力，在強風下角柱或接頭可能先達到容量；同時高估中段柱的參與，使實際側向變位與樓板翹曲大於預期，帷幕牆接縫也被額外拉扯。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring shear lag underestimates axial forces in corner columns and their joints, which may reach capacity first in strong wind; it also overestimates the contribution of mid-face columns, so real drift and floor warping exceed predictions and façade joints are strained further. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在三維框架模型中比較單一大管與九管束筒在同一風荷載下的翼板柱軸力分布，計算角柱與中段柱的軸力比作為剪力遲滯指標，並把剪力與彎曲兩部分的頂部變位拆開檢討。","textEn":"In a three-dimensional frame model compare flange-column axial forces for one large tube and for the nine-tube bundle under the same wind load, use the ratio of corner to mid-face column force as a shear-lag index, and separate the shear and bending components of top drift.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"檢核框管時要以完整三維模型而非平面等效梁取得角柱設計力，並把角柱、角隅接頭與內部框架交會柱列為加強檢驗的構件類別。","textEn":"Check framed tubes with a full three-dimensional model rather than an equivalent plane beam to obtain corner-column design forces, and place corner columns, corner joints and columns where interior frames intersect in an enhanced inspection category.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「束筒與剪力遲滯」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bundled tubes and shear lag\"?","options":["在三維框架模型中比較單一大管與九管束筒在同一風荷載下的翼板柱軸力分布，計算角柱與中段柱的軸力比作為剪力遲滯指標，並把剪力與彎曲兩部分的頂部變位拆開檢討。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。"],"optionsEn":["In a three-dimensional frame model compare flange-column axial forces for one large tube and for the nine-tube bundle under the same wind load, use the ratio of corner to mid-face column force as a shear-lag index, and separate the shear and bending components of top drift.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在三維框架模型中比較單一大管與九管束筒在同一風荷載下的翼板柱軸力分布，計算角柱與中段柱的軸力比作為剪力遲滯指標，並把剪力與彎曲兩部分的頂部變位拆開檢討。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"In a three-dimensional frame model compare flange-column axial forces for one large tube and for the nine-tube bundle under the same wind load, use the ratio of corner to mid-face column force as a shear-lag index, and separate the shear and bending components of top drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b028-v13-04","title":"束筒與剪力遲滯：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bundled tubes and shear lag: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「九管束筒與內部腹板」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Nine bundled tubes and interior webs” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略剪力遲滯會低估角柱與其接頭的軸力，在強風下角柱或接頭可能先達到容量；同時高估中段柱的參與，使實際側向變位與樓板翹曲大於預期，帷幕牆接縫也被額外拉扯。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring shear lag underestimates axial forces in corner columns and their joints, which may reach capacity first in strong wind; it also overestimates the contribution of mid-face columns, so real drift and floor warping exceed predictions and façade joints are strained further. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：束筒在 225 ft 見方的平面中多加兩道縱橫向內部框架，把翼板分成三段、腹板由兩道增為四道，使軸力分布更均勻，剪力勁度也加倍。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The bundled tube adds two interior frames in each direction within the 225 ft square, splitting each flange into three segments and doubling the web frames from two to four, which evens out axial forces and doubles shear stiffness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略剪力遲滯會低估角柱與其接頭的軸力，在強風下角柱或接頭可能先達到容量；同時高估中段柱的參與，使實際側向變位與樓板翹曲大於預期，帷幕牆接縫也被額外拉扯。","textEn":"Ignoring shear lag underestimates axial forces in corner columns and their joints, which may reach capacity first in strong wind; it also overestimates the contribution of mid-face columns, so real drift and floor warping exceed predictions and façade joints are strained further.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「束筒與剪力遲滯」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bundled tubes and shear lag\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略剪力遲滯會低估角柱與其接頭的軸力，在強風下角柱或接頭可能先達到容量；同時高估中段柱的參與，使實際側向變位與樓板翹曲大於預期，帷幕牆接縫也被額外拉扯。","收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Ignoring shear lag underestimates axial forces in corner columns and their joints, which may reach capacity first in strong wind.","Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略剪力遲滯會低估角柱與其接頭的軸力，在強風下角柱或接頭可能先達到容量；同時高估中段柱的參與，使實際側向變位與樓板翹曲大於預期，帷幕牆接縫也被額外拉扯。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring shear lag underestimates axial forces in corner columns and their joints, which may reach capacity first in strong wind; it also overestimates the contribution of mid-face columns, so real drift and floor warping exceed predictions and façade joints are strained further. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b028-v13-05","title":"管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「50／66／90 層分段收進」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Setbacks at floors 50, 66 and 90” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"九管全部升到 50 層，西北與東南兩管在此終止；東北與西南兩管在 66 層終止，形成十字形平面；北、東、南三管在 90 層終止，只剩西管與中央管到 108 層。逐段減少的樓板面積讓質量集中在下部，降低地震與風致慣性力的力臂，也讓不同高度的寬度變化擾亂渦流脫落。代價是 90 層以上只剩兩管，平面不再雙軸對稱，質心與剛心產生偏移，上部需要處理扭轉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「50／66／90 層分段收進」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"All nine tubes rise to floor 50, where the northwest and southeast tubes stop; the northeast and southwest tubes stop at floor 66, leaving a cruciform plan; the north, east and south tubes stop at floor 90, leaving only the west and centre tubes to floor 108. The shrinking floor area concentrates mass low down, shortening the lever arm of seismic and wind-induced inertia forces, and the width changes disrupt vortex shedding along the height. The price is that above floor 90 only two tubes remain, the plan loses double symmetry, the centres of mass and stiffness separate, and the upper levels must handle torsion. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Setbacks at floors 50, 66 and 90” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以每管每層為一單位，層高 3.91 m：1–50 層 450 單位，中點 97.8 m；51–66 層 112 單位，226.8 m；67–90 層 120 單位，305.0 m；91–108 層 36 單位，387.1 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Count one unit per tube per floor with a 3.91 m storey: floors 1–50 give 450 units at a mid-height of 97.8 m, floors 51–66 give 112 at 226.8 m, floors 67–90 give 120 at 305.0 m and floors 91–108 give 36 at 387.1 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「50／66／90 層分段收進」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Setbacks at floors 50, 66 and 90”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-05-k1","title":"管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉","titleEn":"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion","text":"九管全部升到 50 層，西北與東南兩管在此終止；東北與西南兩管在 66 層終止，形成十字形平面；北、東、南三管在 90 層終止，只剩西管與中央管到 108 層。逐段減少的樓板面積讓質量集中在下部，降低地震與風致慣性力的力臂，也讓不同高度的寬度變化擾亂渦流脫落。","textEn":"All nine tubes rise to floor 50, where the northwest and southeast tubes stop; the northeast and southwest tubes stop at floor 66, leaving a cruciform plan; the north, east and south tubes stop at floor 90, leaving only the west and centre tubes to floor 108. The shrinking floor area concentrates mass low down, shortening the lever arm of seismic and wind-induced inertia forces, and the width changes disrupt vortex shedding along the height.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion\" is correct?","options":["收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。","框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。","九管全部升到 50 層，西北與東南兩管在此終止；東北與西南兩管在 66 層終止，形成十字形平面；北、東、南三管在 90 層終止，只剩西管與中央管到 108 層。"],"optionsEn":["Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour.","A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters.","All nine tubes rise to floor 50, where the northwest and southeast tubes stop."],"answer":2,"explanation":"九管全部升到 50 層，西北與東南兩管在此終止；東北與西南兩管在 66 層終止，形成十字形平面；北、東、南三管在 90 層終止，只剩西管與中央管到 108 層。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"All nine tubes rise to floor 50, where the northwest and southeast tubes stop; the northeast and southwest tubes stop at floor 66, leaving a cruciform plan; the north, east and south tubes stop at floor 90, leaving only the west and centre tubes to floor 108. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b028-v13-06","title":"管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉：定量估算","titleEn":"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「50／66／90 層分段收進」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Setbacks at floors 50, 66 and 90” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以每管每層為一單位，層高 3.91 m：1–50 層 450 單位，中點 97.8 m；51–66 層 112 單位，226.8 m；67–90 層 120 單位，305.0 m；91–108 層 36 單位，387.1 m。質心高度 z = (450×97.8 + 112×226.8 + 120×305.0 + 36×387.1)/718 ≈ 167 m；若九管都到 108 層，z = 211 m，收進使質心降低約 21%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Count one unit per tube per floor with a 3.91 m storey: floors 1–50 give 450 units at a mid-height of 97.8 m, floors 51–66 give 112 at 226.8 m, floors 67–90 give 120 at 305.0 m and floors 91–108 give 36 at 387.1 m. The centroid height z = (450×97.8 + 112×226.8 + 120×305.0 + 36×387.1)/718 ≈ 167 m; with all nine tubes to floor 108, z = 211 m, so the setbacks lower the centroid by about 21%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從模型取出各樓層質心與剛心位置，檢查 90 層以上的偏心距與扭轉振態的頻率與參與質量；風洞試驗則需量測扭矩頻譜，確認上部扭轉造成的角落加速度在居住性準則內。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Extract the centres of mass and stiffness at each floor from the model, checking the eccentricity above floor 90 and the frequency and participating mass of torsional modes; the wind-tunnel test must measure torque spectra to confirm that corner accelerations from upper-level torsion meet habitability criteria.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以每管每層為一單位，層高 3.91 m：1–50 層 450 單位，中點 97.8 m；51–66 層 112 單位，226.8 m；67–90 層 120 單位，305.0 m；91–108 層 36 單位，387.1 m。質心高度 z = (450×97.8 + 112×226.8 + 120×305.0 + 36×387.1)/718 ≈ 167 m；若九管都到 108 層，z = 211 m，收進使質心降低約 21%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Count one unit per tube per floor with a 3.91 m storey: floors 1–50 give 450 units at a mid-height of 97.8 m, floors 51–66 give 112 at 226.8 m, floors 67–90 give 120 at 305.0 m and floors 91–108 give 36 at 387.1 m. The centroid height z = (450×97.8 + 112×226.8 + 120×305.0 + 36×387.1)/718 ≈ 167 m; with all nine tubes to floor 108, z = 211 m, so the setbacks lower the centroid by about 21%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion\", which statement holds?","options":["以每管每層為一單位，層高 3.91 m：1–50 層 450 單位，中點 97.8 m。","鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。","規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。"],"optionsEn":["Count one unit per tube per floor with a 3.91 m storey: floors 1–50 give 450 units at a mid-height of 97.8 m, floors 51–66 give 112 at 226.8 m, floors 67–90 give 120 at 305.0 m and floors 91–108 give 36 at 387.1 m.","Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers.","Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以每管每層為一單位，層高 3.91 m：1–50 層 450 單位，中點 97.8 m；51–66 層 112 單位，226.8 m；67–90 層 120 單位，305.0 m；91–108 層 36 單位，387.1 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Count one unit per tube per floor with a 3.91 m storey: floors 1–50 give 450 units at a mid-height of 97.8 m, floors 51–66 give 112 at 226.8 m, floors 67–90 give 120 at 305.0 m and floors 91–108 give 36 at 387.1 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b028-v13-07","title":"管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「50／66／90 層分段收進」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Setbacks at floors 50, 66 and 90” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從模型取出各樓層質心與剛心位置，檢查 90 層以上的偏心距與扭轉振態的頻率與參與質量；風洞試驗則需量測扭矩頻譜，確認上部扭轉造成的角落加速度在居住性準則內。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Extract the centres of mass and stiffness at each floor from the model, checking the eccentricity above floor 90 and the frequency and participating mass of torsional modes; the wind-tunnel test must measure torque spectra to confirm that corner accelerations from upper-level torsion meet habitability criteria. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：收進樓層應列為結構檢核重點：樓板厚度與配筋、帶狀桁架或深梁的剪力傳遞、終止柱的錨定細部，並要求風洞報告分別列出順風、橫風與扭轉反應。","observationEn":"Site practice: Treat setback floors as key structural checkpoints for slab thickness and reinforcement, shear transfer through belt trusses or deep beams and anchorage of terminating columns, and require the wind-tunnel report to list along-wind, across-wind and torsional responses separately.","failure":"注意干擾：若收進處的樓板與帶狀構件沒有足夠的剪力傳遞能力，終止管筒的柱力無法順利交給相鄰管筒，造成局部應力集中；上部扭轉若被低估，角落辦公室會感受到明顯旋轉擺動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If floors and belt members at a setback cannot transfer enough shear, forces from terminating tubes cannot pass smoothly to neighbouring tubes and stresses concentrate locally; if upper-level torsion is underestimated, corner offices feel noticeable twisting motion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從模型取出各樓層質心與剛心位置，檢查 90 層以上的偏心距與扭轉振態的頻率與參與質量；風洞試驗則需量測扭矩頻譜，確認上部扭轉造成的角落加速度在居住性準則內。","textEn":"Extract the centres of mass and stiffness at each floor from the model, checking the eccentricity above floor 90 and the frequency and participating mass of torsional modes; the wind-tunnel test must measure torque spectra to confirm that corner accelerations from upper-level torsion meet habitability criteria.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"收進樓層應列為結構檢核重點：樓板厚度與配筋、帶狀桁架或深梁的剪力傳遞、終止柱的錨定細部，並要求風洞報告分別列出順風、橫風與扭轉反應。","textEn":"Treat setback floors as key structural checkpoints for slab thickness and reinforcement, shear transfer through belt trusses or deep beams and anchorage of terminating columns, and require the wind-tunnel report to list along-wind, across-wind and torsional responses separately.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","從模型取出各樓層質心與剛心位置，檢查 90 層以上的偏心距與扭轉振態的頻率與參與質量；風洞試驗則需量測扭矩頻譜，確認上部扭轉造成的角落加速度在居住性準則內。","在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Extract the centres of mass and stiffness at each floor from the model, checking the eccentricity above floor 90 and the frequency and participating mass of torsional modes.","Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從模型取出各樓層質心與剛心位置，檢查 90 層以上的偏心距與扭轉振態的頻率與參與質量；風洞試驗則需量測扭矩頻譜，確認上部扭轉造成的角落加速度在居住性準則內。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Extract the centres of mass and stiffness at each floor from the model, checking the eccentricity above floor 90 and the frequency and participating mass of torsional modes; the wind-tunnel test must measure torque spectra to confirm that corner accelerations from upper-level torsion meet habitability criteria. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b028-v13-08","title":"管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉：失效診斷","titleEn":"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「50／66／90 層分段收進」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Setbacks at floors 50, 66 and 90” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若收進處的樓板與帶狀構件沒有足夠的剪力傳遞能力，終止管筒的柱力無法順利交給相鄰管筒，造成局部應力集中；上部扭轉若被低估，角落辦公室會感受到明顯旋轉擺動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If floors and belt members at a setback cannot transfer enough shear, forces from terminating tubes cannot pass smoothly to neighbouring tubes and stresses concentrate locally; if upper-level torsion is underestimated, corner offices feel noticeable twisting motion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：代價是 90 層以上只剩兩管，平面不再雙軸對稱，質心與剛心產生偏移，上部需要處理扭轉。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The price is that above floor 90 only two tubes remain, the plan loses double symmetry, the centres of mass and stiffness separate, and the upper levels must handle torsion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若收進處的樓板與帶狀構件沒有足夠的剪力傳遞能力，終止管筒的柱力無法順利交給相鄰管筒，造成局部應力集中；上部扭轉若被低估，角落辦公室會感受到明顯旋轉擺動。","textEn":"If floors and belt members at a setback cannot transfer enough shear, forces from terminating tubes cannot pass smoothly to neighbouring tubes and stresses concentrate locally; if upper-level torsion is underestimated, corner offices feel noticeable twisting motion.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「管筒分段終止、質心與扭轉」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Staged tube terminations, mass centroid and torsion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。","若收進處的樓板與帶狀構件沒有足夠的剪力傳遞能力，終止管筒的柱力無法順利交給相鄰管筒，造成局部應力集中；上部扭轉若被低估，角落辦公室會感受到明顯旋轉擺動。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters.","If floors and belt members at a setback cannot transfer enough shear, forces from terminating tubes cannot pass smoothly to neighbouring tubes and stresses concentrate locally."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若收進處的樓板與帶狀構件沒有足夠的剪力傳遞能力，終止管筒的柱力無法順利交給相鄰管筒，造成局部應力集中；上部扭轉若被低估，角落辦公室會感受到明顯旋轉擺動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If floors and belt members at a setback cannot transfer enough shear, forces from terminating tubes cannot pass smoothly to neighbouring tubes and stresses concentrate locally; if upper-level torsion is underestimated, corner offices feel noticeable twisting motion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b028-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「密柱框管的構件與預組單元」與「長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube\" and \"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b028-v13-09","title":"密柱框管的構件與預組單元：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「15 ft 柱距框管與裙梁」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “15 ft column module and spandrels” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"每個管筒的周邊柱以 15 ft（約 4.57 m）為模組，與深裙梁剛接成近似穿孔牆的框架。在側力下，裙梁兩端承受相反方向的彎矩，反曲點大約在跨中，跨中彎矩接近零，剪力則沿跨長大致固定；柱段與部分裙梁可在工廠預組，現場只做接合，減少高空焊接。SOM 說明鋼構先預組成段件再於現場以螺栓接合，柱段為兩層樓高。剛接框管的勁度主要由裙梁的彎曲與剪力勁度決定，因此裙梁深度與接頭剛度是控制參數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「15 ft 柱距框管與裙梁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each tube's perimeter columns follow a 15 ft (about 4.57 m) module and are rigidly framed with deep spandrels into something close to a perforated wall. Under lateral load the spandrel ends bend in opposite directions, the point of contraflexure sits near mid-span where moment is nearly zero and shear is constant; column segments and parts of spandrels can be pre-assembled in the shop so the site only makes connections, reducing welding at height. SOM describes the steel as pre-assembled into sections and bolted together on site, with column pieces two storeys tall. Tube stiffness depends mainly on spandrel bending and shear stiffness, so spandrel depth and joint rigidity are the controlling parameters. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “15 ft column module and spandrels” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：反對稱彎矩下裙梁剪力 V = 2M/L。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Under antisymmetric bending the spandrel shear is V = 2M/L.","failure":"常見誤解：「框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「15 ft 柱距框管與裙梁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “15 ft column module and spandrels”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-09-k1","title":"密柱框管的構件與預組單元","titleEn":"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube","text":"每個管筒的周邊柱以 15 ft（約 4.57 m）為模組，與深裙梁剛接成近似穿孔牆的框架。在側力下，裙梁兩端承受相反方向的彎矩，反曲點大約在跨中，跨中彎矩接近零，剪力則沿跨長大致固定；柱段與部分裙梁可在工廠預組，現場只做接合，減少高空焊接。","textEn":"Each tube's perimeter columns follow a 15 ft (about 4.57 m) module and are rigidly framed with deep spandrels into something close to a perforated wall. Under lateral load the spandrel ends bend in opposite directions, the point of contraflexure sits near mid-span where moment is nearly zero and shear is constant; column segments and parts of spandrels can be pre-assembled in the shop so the site only makes connections, reducing welding at height.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「密柱框管的構件與預組單元」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube\" is correct?","options":["每個管筒的周邊柱以 15 ft（約 4.57 m）為模組，與深裙梁剛接成近似穿孔牆的框架。","框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。","樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。"],"optionsEn":["Each tube's perimeter columns follow a 15 ft (about 4.57 m) module and are rigidly framed with deep spandrels into something close to a perforated wall.","A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters.","If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個管筒的周邊柱以 15 ft（約 4.57 m）為模組，與深裙梁剛接成近似穿孔牆的框架。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each tube's perimeter columns follow a 15 ft (about 4.57 m) module and are rigidly framed with deep spandrels into something close to a perforated wall. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b028-v13-10","title":"密柱框管的構件與預組單元：定量估算","titleEn":"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「15 ft 柱距框管與裙梁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “15 ft column module and spandrels” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：反對稱彎矩下裙梁剪力 V = 2M/L。若柱面處裙梁端彎矩 M = 600 kN·m、柱距 L = 4.57 m，V = 2×600/4.57 ≈ 263 kN；在反曲點附近設置螺栓續接時，主要傳遞 263 kN 的剪力與很小的彎矩。數值為教學假設，以柱心距近似淨跨。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Under antisymmetric bending the spandrel shear is V = 2M/L. With an end moment M = 600 kN·m at the column face and a column spacing L = 4.57 m, V = 2×600/4.57 ≈ 263 kN; a bolted splice near the contraflexure point mainly carries this 263 kN shear and very little moment. Values are teaching assumptions using the centre spacing as an approximation of the clear span. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：工廠預組單元出廠前檢查柱段長度、裙梁位置與孔位，以樣板或三維量測確認累積誤差；現場螺栓接合依規範抽驗預拉力，並在每組樓層完成後量測柱垂直度與樓層標高。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before shop-assembled units leave the plant, check column length, spandrel position and hole locations with templates or three-dimensional measurement to control cumulative error; on site sample bolt pretension to the specification and survey column plumbness and floor levels after each tier.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"反對稱彎矩下裙梁剪力 V = 2M/L。若柱面處裙梁端彎矩 M = 600 kN·m、柱距 L = 4.57 m，V = 2×600/4.57 ≈ 263 kN；在反曲點附近設置螺栓續接時，主要傳遞 263 kN 的剪力與很小的彎矩。數值為教學假設，以柱心距近似淨跨。","textEn":"Under antisymmetric bending the spandrel shear is V = 2M/L. With an end moment M = 600 kN·m at the column face and a column spacing L = 4.57 m, V = 2×600/4.57 ≈ 263 kN; a bolted splice near the contraflexure point mainly carries this 263 kN shear and very little moment. Values are teaching assumptions using the centre spacing as an approximation of the clear span.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「密柱框管的構件與預組單元」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube\", which statement holds?","options":["沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。","反對稱彎矩下裙梁剪力 V = 2M/L。","帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。"],"optionsEn":["A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.","Under antisymmetric bending the spandrel shear is V = 2M/L.","The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反對稱彎矩下裙梁剪力 V = 2M/L。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Under antisymmetric bending the spandrel shear is V = 2M/L. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b028-v13-11","title":"密柱框管的構件與預組單元：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「15 ft 柱距框管與裙梁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “15 ft column module and spandrels” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"工廠預組單元出廠前檢查柱段長度、裙梁位置與孔位，以樣板或三維量測確認累積誤差；現場螺栓接合依規範抽驗預拉力，並在每組樓層完成後量測柱垂直度與樓層標高。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before shop-assembled units leave the plant, check column length, spandrel position and hole locations with templates or three-dimensional measurement to control cumulative error; on site sample bolt pretension to the specification and survey column plumbness and floor levels after each tier. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：預組單元的分段位置應由結構工程師依彎矩圖確認，並規定工廠與現場的尺寸允差及量測紀錄格式；裙梁開孔或切割一律需結構審查。","observationEn":"Site practice: The structural engineer should confirm splice locations of prefabricated units against the moment diagram, set shop and site dimensional tolerances with a standard record format, and require structural review for any spandrel opening or cut.","failure":"注意干擾：續接若設在彎矩較大的位置卻只按剪力設計，強風下螺栓群會滑移並使框管勁度下降；預組單元尺寸誤差累積則讓上部柱與下部柱偏心接合，增加附加彎矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A splice placed where moment is significant but designed only for shear lets the bolt group slip in strong wind and softens the tube; accumulated dimensional errors in prefabricated units make upper and lower columns meet eccentrically, adding secondary moments. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"工廠預組單元出廠前檢查柱段長度、裙梁位置與孔位，以樣板或三維量測確認累積誤差；現場螺栓接合依規範抽驗預拉力，並在每組樓層完成後量測柱垂直度與樓層標高。","textEn":"Before shop-assembled units leave the plant, check column length, spandrel position and hole locations with templates or three-dimensional measurement to control cumulative error; on site sample bolt pretension to the specification and survey column plumbness and floor levels after each tier.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"預組單元的分段位置應由結構工程師依彎矩圖確認，並規定工廠與現場的尺寸允差及量測紀錄格式；裙梁開孔或切割一律需結構審查。","textEn":"The structural engineer should confirm splice locations of prefabricated units against the moment diagram, set shop and site dimensional tolerances with a standard record format, and require structural review for any spandrel opening or cut.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「密柱框管的構件與預組單元」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。","工廠預組單元出廠前檢查柱段長度、裙梁位置與孔位，以樣板或三維量測確認累積誤差；現場螺栓接合依規範抽驗預拉力，並在每組樓層完成後量測柱垂直度與樓層標高。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity.","Before shop-assembled units leave the plant, check column length, spandrel position and hole locations with templates or three-dimensional measurement to control cumulative error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"工廠預組單元出廠前檢查柱段長度、裙梁位置與孔位，以樣板或三維量測確認累積誤差；現場螺栓接合依規範抽驗預拉力，並在每組樓層完成後量測柱垂直度與樓層標高。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before shop-assembled units leave the plant, check column length, spandrel position and hole locations with templates or three-dimensional measurement to control cumulative error; on site sample bolt pretension to the specification and survey column plumbness and floor levels after each tier. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b028-v13-12","title":"密柱框管的構件與預組單元：失效診斷","titleEn":"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「15 ft 柱距框管與裙梁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “15 ft column module and spandrels” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"續接若設在彎矩較大的位置卻只按剪力設計，強風下螺栓群會滑移並使框管勁度下降；預組單元尺寸誤差累積則讓上部柱與下部柱偏心接合，增加附加彎矩。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A splice placed where moment is significant but designed only for shear lets the bolt group slip in strong wind and softens the tube; accumulated dimensional errors in prefabricated units make upper and lower columns meet eccentrically, adding secondary moments. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：剛接框管的勁度主要由裙梁的彎曲與剪力勁度決定，因此裙梁深度與接頭剛度是控制參數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Tube stiffness depends mainly on spandrel bending and shear stiffness, so spandrel depth and joint rigidity are the controlling parameters.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"續接若設在彎矩較大的位置卻只按剪力設計，強風下螺栓群會滑移並使框管勁度下降；預組單元尺寸誤差累積則讓上部柱與下部柱偏心接合，增加附加彎矩。","textEn":"A splice placed where moment is significant but designed only for shear lets the bolt group slip in strong wind and softens the tube; accumulated dimensional errors in prefabricated units make upper and lower columns meet eccentrically, adding secondary moments.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「密柱框管的構件與預組單元」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Members and prefabricated units of the dense-column tube\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["續接若設在彎矩較大的位置卻只按剪力設計，強風下螺栓群會滑移並使框管勁度下降；預組單元尺寸誤差累積則讓上部柱與下部柱偏心接合，增加附加彎矩。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。"],"optionsEn":["A splice placed where moment is significant but designed only for shear lets the bolt group slip in strong wind and softens the tube.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"續接若設在彎矩較大的位置卻只按剪力設計，強風下螺栓群會滑移並使框管勁度下降；預組單元尺寸誤差累積則讓上部柱與下部柱偏心接合，增加附加彎矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A splice placed where moment is significant but designed only for shear lets the bolt group slip in strong wind and softens the tube; accumulated dimensional errors in prefabricated units make upper and lower columns meet eccentrically, adding secondary moments. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b028-v13-13","title":"長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「75 ft 複合樓板桁架」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “75 ft composite floor trusses” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"每個管筒內部無柱，樓板以跨度 75 ft（22.9 m）、深 40 in（1.02 m）的華倫式桁架、間距 15 ft 支承，桁架以只傳剪力的高強螺栓接到柱上，視為簡支。樓板為 3 in 壓型鋼板加 2½ in 輕質混凝土，以 ¾ in 剪力釘形成複合作用；角隅管筒每六層交替桁架方向，讓管壁受力平均。複合作用使混凝土板承壓、桁架下弦受拉，剪力釘必須把兩者間的水平力完整傳遞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「75 ft 複合樓板桁架」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each tube is column-free inside: floors are carried by Warren trusses 75 ft (22.9 m) long and 40 in (1.02 m) deep at 15 ft centres, bolted to columns with high-strength bolts designed for shear only, so they are simply supported. The slab is a 3 in metal deck with 2½ in of lightweight concrete, made composite with ¾ in shear studs; in the corner tubes the truss direction alternates every six floors to balance load on the tube walls. Composite action puts the slab in compression and the bottom chord in tension, and the studs must transfer the full horizontal force between them. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “75 ft composite floor trusses” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m，L = 22.86 m：M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m；有效力臂約 1.10 m 時弦力 C = T ≈ 1,465 kN；每支剪力釘 Q_n 取 70 kN，半跨需約 21 支，全跨約 42 支。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m and L = 22.86 m give M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m; with an effective lever arm of about 1.10 m the chord force is C = T ≈ 1,465 kN; at Q_n = 70 kN per stud, about 21 studs are needed per half span, about 42 per truss.","failure":"常見誤解：「樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「75 ft 複合樓板桁架」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “75 ft composite floor trusses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-13-k1","title":"長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘","titleEn":"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs","text":"每個管筒內部無柱，樓板以跨度 75 ft（22.9 m）、深 40 in（1.02 m）的華倫式桁架、間距 15 ft 支承，桁架以只傳剪力的高強螺栓接到柱上，視為簡支。樓板為 3 in 壓型鋼板加 2½ in 輕質混凝土，以 ¾ in 剪力釘形成複合作用；角隅管筒每六層交替桁架方向，讓管壁受力平均。","textEn":"Each tube is column-free inside: floors are carried by Warren trusses 75 ft (22.9 m) long and 40 in (1.02 m) deep at 15 ft centres, bolted to columns with high-strength bolts designed for shear only, so they are simply supported. The slab is a 3 in metal deck with 2½ in of lightweight concrete, made composite with ¾ in shear studs; in the corner tubes the truss direction alternates every six floors to balance load on the tube walls.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs\" is correct?","options":["樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。","每個管筒內部無柱，樓板以跨度 75 ft（22.9 m）、深 40 in（1.02 m）的華倫式桁架、間距 15 ft 支承，桁架以只傳剪力的高強螺栓接到柱上，視為簡支。","鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。"],"optionsEn":["If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour.","Each tube is column-free inside: floors are carried by Warren trusses 75 ft (22.9 m) long and 40 in (1.02 m) deep at 15 ft centres, bolted to columns with high-strength bolts designed for shear only, so they are simply supported.","Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每個管筒內部無柱，樓板以跨度 75 ft（22.9 m）、深 40 in（1.02 m）的華倫式桁架、間距 15 ft 支承，桁架以只傳剪力的高強螺栓接到柱上，視為簡支。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each tube is column-free inside: floors are carried by Warren trusses 75 ft (22.9 m) long and 40 in (1.02 m) deep at 15 ft centres, bolted to columns with high-strength bolts designed for shear only, so they are simply supported. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b028-v13-14","title":"長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「75 ft 複合樓板桁架」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “75 ft composite floor trusses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m，L = 22.86 m：M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m；有效力臂約 1.10 m 時弦力 C = T ≈ 1,465 kN；每支剪力釘 Q_n 取 70 kN，半跨需約 21 支，全跨約 42 支。跨深比 22.86/1.016 ≈ 22.5。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m and L = 22.86 m give M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m; with an effective lever arm of about 1.10 m the chord force is C = T ≈ 1,465 kN; at Q_n = 70 kN per stud, about 21 studs are needed per half span, about 42 per truss. The span-to-depth ratio is 22.86/1.016 ≈ 22.5. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：剪力釘焊接後依 AWS D1.1 做彎曲試驗抽驗（敲彎 15° 不得斷裂）並檢查焊趾完整；桁架出廠前做尺寸與焊道檢驗，安裝後量測樓板撓度並以腳步激振量測樓板頻率，與設計預測比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After stud welding, bend-test a sample to AWS D1.1 (bent 15° without failure) and inspect weld collars; check truss dimensions and welds before delivery, and after erection measure slab deflection and floor frequency under heel-drop excitation for comparison with design predictions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m，L = 22.86 m：M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m；有效力臂約 1.10 m 時弦力 C = T ≈ 1,465 kN；每支剪力釘 Q_n 取 70 kN，半跨需約 21 支，全跨約 42 支。跨深比 22.86/1.016 ≈ 22.5。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m and L = 22.86 m give M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m; with an effective lever arm of about 1.10 m the chord force is C = T ≈ 1,465 kN; at Q_n = 70 kN per stud, about 21 studs are needed per half span, about 42 per truss. The span-to-depth ratio is 22.86/1.016 ≈ 22.5. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs\", which statement holds?","options":["規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。","在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。","w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m，L = 22.86 m：M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m。"],"optionsEn":["Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower.","Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk.","w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m and L = 22.86 m give M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m，L = 22.86 m：M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m；有效力臂約 1.10 m 時弦力 C = T ≈ 1,465 kN；每支剪力釘 Q_n 取 70 kN，半跨需約 21 支，全跨約 42 支。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"w = (3.0 + 2.4) kPa×4.57 m ≈ 24.7 kN/m and L = 22.86 m give M = wL²/8 ≈ 1,612 kN·m; with an effective lever arm of about 1.10 m the chord force is C = T ≈ 1,465 kN; at Q_n = 70 kN per stud, about 21 studs are needed per half span, about 42 per truss. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b028-v13-15","title":"長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「75 ft 複合樓板桁架」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “75 ft composite floor trusses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"剪力釘焊接後依 AWS D1.1 做彎曲試驗抽驗（敲彎 15° 不得斷裂）並檢查焊趾完整；桁架出廠前做尺寸與焊道檢驗，安裝後量測樓板撓度並以腳步激振量測樓板頻率，與設計預測比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After stud welding, bend-test a sample to AWS D1.1 (bent 15° without failure) and inspect weld collars; check truss dimensions and welds before delivery, and after erection measure slab deflection and floor frequency under heel-drop excitation for comparison with design predictions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：剪力釘施工前須做程序試焊並每日開工試驗，雨後或有積水時暫停焊接；樓板開孔改裝時，結構工程師須確認剪力釘與桁架弦桿未被破壞。","observationEn":"Site practice: Qualify the stud-welding procedure before production and run daily start-up tests, suspending welding after rain or with standing water; for later slab openings, the structural engineer must confirm that studs and truss chords are not damaged.","failure":"注意干擾：剪力釘數量或焊接品質不足時，樓板與桁架間發生滑移，複合勁度降低，撓度與樓板振動都增加；在壓型鋼板上焊釘若鍍鋅層或積水處理不當，焊接不良率會明顯上升。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Too few studs or poor welds let the slab slip on the truss, reducing composite stiffness and increasing deflection and floor vibration; welding through metal deck with poorly managed galvanising or standing water raises the defect rate sharply. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"剪力釘焊接後依 AWS D1.1 做彎曲試驗抽驗（敲彎 15° 不得斷裂）並檢查焊趾完整；桁架出廠前做尺寸與焊道檢驗，安裝後量測樓板撓度並以腳步激振量測樓板頻率，與設計預測比較。","textEn":"After stud welding, bend-test a sample to AWS D1.1 (bent 15° without failure) and inspect weld collars; check truss dimensions and welds before delivery, and after erection measure slab deflection and floor frequency under heel-drop excitation for comparison with design predictions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"剪力釘施工前須做程序試焊並每日開工試驗，雨後或有積水時暫停焊接；樓板開孔改裝時，結構工程師須確認剪力釘與桁架弦桿未被破壞。","textEn":"Qualify the stud-welding procedure before production and run daily start-up tests, suspending welding after rain or with standing water; for later slab openings, the structural engineer must confirm that studs and truss chords are not damaged.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs\"?","options":["剪力釘焊接後依 AWS D1.1 做彎曲試驗抽驗（敲彎 15° 不得斷裂）並檢查焊趾完整。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。"],"optionsEn":["After stud welding, bend-test a sample to AWS D1.1 (bent 15° without failure) and inspect weld collars.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally."],"answer":0,"explanation":"剪力釘焊接後依 AWS D1.1 做彎曲試驗抽驗（敲彎 15° 不得斷裂）並檢查焊趾完整；桁架出廠前做尺寸與焊道檢驗，安裝後量測樓板撓度並以腳步激振量測樓板頻率，與設計預測比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After stud welding, bend-test a sample to AWS D1.1 (bent 15° without failure) and inspect weld collars; check truss dimensions and welds before delivery, and after erection measure slab deflection and floor frequency under heel-drop excitation for comparison with design predictions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b028-v13-16","title":"長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「75 ft 複合樓板桁架」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “75 ft composite floor trusses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"剪力釘數量或焊接品質不足時，樓板與桁架間發生滑移，複合勁度降低，撓度與樓板振動都增加；在壓型鋼板上焊釘若鍍鋅層或積水處理不當，焊接不良率會明顯上升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Too few studs or poor welds let the slab slip on the truss, reducing composite stiffness and increasing deflection and floor vibration; welding through metal deck with poorly managed galvanising or standing water raises the defect rate sharply. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：複合作用使混凝土板承壓、桁架下弦受拉，剪力釘必須把兩者間的水平力完整傳遞。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Composite action puts the slab in compression and the bottom chord in tension, and the studs must transfer the full horizontal force between them.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"剪力釘數量或焊接品質不足時，樓板與桁架間發生滑移，複合勁度降低，撓度與樓板振動都增加；在壓型鋼板上焊釘若鍍鋅層或積水處理不當，焊接不良率會明顯上升。","textEn":"Too few studs or poor welds let the slab slip on the truss, reducing composite stiffness and increasing deflection and floor vibration; welding through metal deck with poorly managed galvanising or standing water raises the defect rate sharply.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長跨複合樓板桁架與剪力釘」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-span composite floor trusses and studs\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","剪力釘數量或焊接品質不足時，樓板與桁架間發生滑移，複合勁度降低，撓度與樓板振動都增加；在壓型鋼板上焊釘若鍍鋅層或積水處理不當，焊接不良率會明顯上升。","鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Too few studs or poor welds let the slab slip on the truss, reducing composite stiffness and increasing deflection and floor vibration.","Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剪力釘數量或焊接品質不足時，樓板與桁架間發生滑移，複合勁度降低，撓度與樓板振動都增加；在壓型鋼板上焊釘若鍍鋅層或積水處理不當，焊接不良率會明顯上升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Too few studs or poor welds let the slab slip on the truss, reducing composite stiffness and increasing deflection and floor vibration; welding through metal deck with poorly managed galvanising or standing water raises the defect rate sharply. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b028-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏」與「深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm\" and \"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b028-v13-17","title":"四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「每週兩層的鋼構安裝」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Steel erection at two floors per week” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公開資料指出施工團隊以每週兩層的速度安裝鋼構，柱段為兩層樓高，待兩層柱就位後才開始安裝樓板構架。基座四周的塔吊直接從卡車吊起鋼料送到安裝位置，鋼料不落地堆放。高速度的關鍵在於重複性：九管相同的 15 ft 模組讓預組單元與樓板桁架高度標準化，吊次、接合與檢驗可以形成固定的循環；同時，接合尚未完成的上部樓層需要臨時穩定，安裝順序必須保證每一節在鎖定前有足夠的側向支撐。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「每週兩層的鋼構安裝」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Public sources report erection at two floors a week, with two-storey column pieces and floor framing starting once two levels of columns were in place. Cranes on all four sides of the base lifted steel straight from delivery trucks into position, so steel never sat on the ground. Speed came from repetition: the identical 15 ft module of all nine tubes standardised the prefabricated units and floor trusses, so lifts, connections and inspections formed a fixed cycle; meanwhile upper tiers with incomplete connections needed temporary stability, so the sequence had to ensure lateral support for each tier before it was locked. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Steel erection at two floors per week” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以總鋼量約 76,000 美噸、110 層估算，每層約 691 美噸；每週兩層即 1,382 美噸。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With about 76,000 short tons of steel over 110 storeys, each floor needs about 691 tons, so two floors a week is 1,382 tons.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「每週兩層的鋼構安裝」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Steel erection at two floors per week”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-17-k1","title":"四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏","titleEn":"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm","text":"公開資料指出施工團隊以每週兩層的速度安裝鋼構，柱段為兩層樓高，待兩層柱就位後才開始安裝樓板構架。基座四周的塔吊直接從卡車吊起鋼料送到安裝位置，鋼料不落地堆放。","textEn":"Public sources report erection at two floors a week, with two-storey column pieces and floor framing starting once two levels of columns were in place. Cranes on all four sides of the base lifted steel straight from delivery trucks into position, so steel never sat on the ground.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm\" is correct?","options":["鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。","沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。","公開資料指出施工團隊以每週兩層的速度安裝鋼構，柱段為兩層樓高，待兩層柱就位後才開始安裝樓板構架。"],"optionsEn":["Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers.","A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.","Public sources report erection at two floors a week, with two-storey column pieces and floor framing starting once two levels of columns were in place."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公開資料指出施工團隊以每週兩層的速度安裝鋼構，柱段為兩層樓高，待兩層柱就位後才開始安裝樓板構架。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Public sources report erection at two floors a week, with two-storey column pieces and floor framing starting once two levels of columns were in place. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b028-v13-18","title":"四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏：定量估算","titleEn":"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「每週兩層的鋼構安裝」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Steel erection at two floors per week” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以總鋼量約 76,000 美噸、110 層估算，每層約 691 美噸；每週兩層即 1,382 美噸。四部塔吊平均每吊 8 美噸，每部每週需 1,382/(4×8) ≈ 43 吊，以每週 5 天計約每天 8.6 吊，另需扣除天候停工的餘裕。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With about 76,000 short tons of steel over 110 storeys, each floor needs about 691 tons, so two floors a week is 1,382 tons. Four cranes lifting an average of 8 tons each need 1,382/(4×8) ≈ 43 lifts per crane per week, about 8.6 a day over five days, before allowing for weather stoppages. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每週以吊次紀錄、到貨序號與安裝順序表比對進度；每節完成後檢查臨時拉索或斜撐、螺栓初鎖數量與柱垂直度，達到規定後才可往上吊裝；強風日依塔吊廠商限制停止吊裝。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track progress weekly by comparing lift logs, delivery piece numbers and the erection sequence; after each tier check temporary guys or braces, the number of snug-tight bolts and column plumbness before lifting higher, and stop lifting in strong wind according to the crane manufacturer's limits.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以總鋼量約 76,000 美噸、110 層估算，每層約 691 美噸；每週兩層即 1,382 美噸。四部塔吊平均每吊 8 美噸，每部每週需 1,382/(4×8) ≈ 43 吊，以每週 5 天計約每天 8.6 吊，另需扣除天候停工的餘裕。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With about 76,000 short tons of steel over 110 storeys, each floor needs about 691 tons, so two floors a week is 1,382 tons. Four cranes lifting an average of 8 tons each need 1,382/(4×8) ≈ 43 lifts per crane per week, about 8.6 a day over five days, before allowing for weather stoppages. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm\", which statement holds?","options":["以總鋼量約 76,000 美噸、110 層估算，每層約 691 美噸；每週兩層即 1,382 美噸。","帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。","裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。"],"optionsEn":["With about 76,000 short tons of steel over 110 storeys, each floor needs about 691 tons, so two floors a week is 1,382 tons.","The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces.","Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以總鋼量約 76,000 美噸、110 層估算，每層約 691 美噸；每週兩層即 1,382 美噸。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With about 76,000 short tons of steel over 110 storeys, each floor needs about 691 tons, so two floors a week is 1,382 tons. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b028-v13-19","title":"四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「每週兩層的鋼構安裝」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Steel erection at two floors per week” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每週以吊次紀錄、到貨序號與安裝順序表比對進度；每節完成後檢查臨時拉索或斜撐、螺栓初鎖數量與柱垂直度，達到規定後才可往上吊裝；強風日依塔吊廠商限制停止吊裝。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track progress weekly by comparing lift logs, delivery piece numbers and the erection sequence; after each tier check temporary guys or braces, the number of snug-tight bolts and column plumbness before lifting higher, and stop lifting in strong wind according to the crane manufacturer's limits. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：安裝計畫須明定每節的最低接合數量、臨時支撐與允許往上安裝的條件，並由鋼構安裝工程師與結構工程師共同簽認；樓板臨時堆放須標示容許荷重。","observationEn":"Site practice: The erection plan must define the minimum connections, temporary bracing and conditions for proceeding upward for each tier, signed by the erection engineer and the structural engineer; temporary storage areas on floors must be marked with allowable loads.","failure":"注意干擾：為了追趕進度而在下層接合未完成前繼續往上吊裝，上部構架可能在強風或吊物碰撞時失穩倒塌；到貨順序錯亂則迫使鋼料臨時堆放在未完成的樓板上，造成超載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Lifting higher before lower connections are finished to catch up on schedule can let the upper frame become unstable in wind or under impact from a load; deliveries out of sequence force steel to be stored on unfinished floors and overload them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每週以吊次紀錄、到貨序號與安裝順序表比對進度；每節完成後檢查臨時拉索或斜撐、螺栓初鎖數量與柱垂直度，達到規定後才可往上吊裝；強風日依塔吊廠商限制停止吊裝。","textEn":"Track progress weekly by comparing lift logs, delivery piece numbers and the erection sequence; after each tier check temporary guys or braces, the number of snug-tight bolts and column plumbness before lifting higher, and stop lifting in strong wind according to the crane manufacturer's limits.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"安裝計畫須明定每節的最低接合數量、臨時支撐與允許往上安裝的條件，並由鋼構安裝工程師與結構工程師共同簽認；樓板臨時堆放須標示容許荷重。","textEn":"The erection plan must define the minimum connections, temporary bracing and conditions for proceeding upward for each tier, signed by the erection engineer and the structural engineer; temporary storage areas on floors must be marked with allowable loads.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","每週以吊次紀錄、到貨序號與安裝順序表比對進度；每節完成後檢查臨時拉索或斜撐、螺栓初鎖數量與柱垂直度，達到規定後才可往上吊裝；強風日依塔吊廠商限制停止吊裝。","收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Track progress weekly by comparing lift logs, delivery piece numbers and the erection sequence.","Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每週以吊次紀錄、到貨序號與安裝順序表比對進度；每節完成後檢查臨時拉索或斜撐、螺栓初鎖數量與柱垂直度，達到規定後才可往上吊裝；強風日依塔吊廠商限制停止吊裝。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track progress weekly by comparing lift logs, delivery piece numbers and the erection sequence; after each tier check temporary guys or braces, the number of snug-tight bolts and column plumbness before lifting higher, and stop lifting in strong wind according to the crane manufacturer's limits. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b028-v13-20","title":"四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏：失效診斷","titleEn":"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「每週兩層的鋼構安裝」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Steel erection at two floors per week” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為了追趕進度而在下層接合未完成前繼續往上吊裝，上部構架可能在強風或吊物碰撞時失穩倒塌；到貨順序錯亂則迫使鋼料臨時堆放在未完成的樓板上，造成超載。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Lifting higher before lower connections are finished to catch up on schedule can let the upper frame become unstable in wind or under impact from a load; deliveries out of sequence force steel to be stored on unfinished floors and overload them. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：高速度的關鍵在於重複性：九管相同的 15 ft 模組讓預組單元與樓板桁架高度標準化，吊次、接合與檢驗可以形成固定的循環；同時，接合尚未完成的上部樓層需要臨時穩定，安裝順序必須保證每一節在鎖定前有足夠的側向支撐。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Speed came from repetition: the identical 15 ft module of all nine tubes standardised the prefabricated units and floor trusses, so lifts, connections and inspections formed a fixed cycle; meanwhile upper tiers with incomplete connections needed temporary stability, so the sequence had to ensure lateral support for each tier before it was locked.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了追趕進度而在下層接合未完成前繼續往上吊裝，上部構架可能在強風或吊物碰撞時失穩倒塌；到貨順序錯亂則迫使鋼料臨時堆放在未完成的樓板上，造成超載。","textEn":"Lifting higher before lower connections are finished to catch up on schedule can let the upper frame become unstable in wind or under impact from a load; deliveries out of sequence force steel to be stored on unfinished floors and overload them.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「四面塔吊與兩層一節的安裝節奏」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Four-side cranes and a two-storey erection rhythm\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。","為了追趕進度而在下層接合未完成前繼續往上吊裝，上部構架可能在強風或吊物碰撞時失穩倒塌；到貨順序錯亂則迫使鋼料臨時堆放在未完成的樓板上，造成超載。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.","Lifting higher before lower connections are finished to catch up on schedule can let the upper frame become unstable in wind or under impact from a load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為了追趕進度而在下層接合未完成前繼續往上吊裝，上部構架可能在強風或吊物碰撞時失穩倒塌；到貨順序錯亂則迫使鋼料臨時堆放在未完成的樓板上，造成超載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Lifting higher before lower connections are finished to catch up on schedule can let the upper frame become unstable in wind or under impact from a load; deliveries out of sequence force steel to be stored on unfinished floors and overload them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b028-v13-21","title":"深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「岩盤嵌入沉箱」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rock-socketed caissons” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"SOM 說明九個管筒坐落在延伸到岩盤的鋼筋混凝土沉箱上；後來的改造資料也指出塔樓沉箱嵌入岩盤，與廣場區的擴底沉箱各自獨立。芝加哥市中心表層為軟弱黏土，岩盤在地表下相當深處，因此柱荷重必須經由沉箱穿過黏土傳到岩層。沉箱的承載包括嵌岩段的側摩擦與底部端承；施工時地下水與黏土擠入會影響孔壁穩定與底部清潔，所以鋼套管與底部檢查是品質的關鍵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「岩盤嵌入沉箱」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"SOM states that the nine tubes rest on reinforced-concrete caissons extending to bedrock, and later renovation records note that the tower caissons are rock-socketed and independent of the belled caissons under the plaza. Downtown Chicago has soft clay near the surface and bedrock at considerable depth, so column loads must pass through the clay to rock via caissons. Capacity comes from side friction in the rock socket and end bearing at the base; during construction groundwater and squeezing clay threaten hole stability and base cleanliness, so steel casings and base inspection are key to quality. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Rock-socketed caissons” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：嵌岩沉箱 Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a rock-socketed caisson Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b.","failure":"常見誤解：「沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「岩盤嵌入沉箱」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Rock-socketed caissons”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-21-k1","title":"深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎","titleEn":"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons","text":"SOM 說明九個管筒坐落在延伸到岩盤的鋼筋混凝土沉箱上；後來的改造資料也指出塔樓沉箱嵌入岩盤，與廣場區的擴底沉箱各自獨立。芝加哥市中心表層為軟弱黏土，岩盤在地表下相當深處，因此柱荷重必須經由沉箱穿過黏土傳到岩層。","textEn":"SOM states that the nine tubes rest on reinforced-concrete caissons extending to bedrock, and later renovation records note that the tower caissons are rock-socketed and independent of the belled caissons under the plaza. Downtown Chicago has soft clay near the surface and bedrock at considerable depth, so column loads must pass through the clay to rock via caissons.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons\" is correct?","options":["SOM 說明九個管筒坐落在延伸到岩盤的鋼筋混凝土沉箱上；後來的改造資料也指出塔樓沉箱嵌入岩盤，與廣場區的擴底沉箱各自獨立。","沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。","規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。"],"optionsEn":["SOM states that the nine tubes rest on reinforced-concrete caissons extending to bedrock, and later renovation records note that the tower caissons are rock-socketed and independent of the belled caissons under the plaza.","A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.","Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"SOM 說明九個管筒坐落在延伸到岩盤的鋼筋混凝土沉箱上；後來的改造資料也指出塔樓沉箱嵌入岩盤，與廣場區的擴底沉箱各自獨立。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"SOM states that the nine tubes rest on reinforced-concrete caissons extending to bedrock, and later renovation records note that the tower caissons are rock-socketed and independent of the belled caissons under the plaza. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b028-v13-22","title":"深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎：定量估算","titleEn":"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岩盤嵌入沉箱」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rock-socketed caissons” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：嵌岩沉箱 Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b。取 D = 3.05 m（10 ft）、嵌岩長 L_s = 3 m、側摩擦 f_s = 1.0 MPa、端承 q_b = 5 MPa：側摩擦 ≈ 28.7 MN、端承 ≈ 36.5 MN，合計約 65.3 MN；以安全係數 2.5 得容許約 26.1 MN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a rock-socketed caisson Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b. With D = 3.05 m (10 ft), a socket length L_s = 3 m, side friction f_s = 1.0 MPa and end bearing q_b = 5 MPa, side friction gives about 28.7 MN and end bearing about 36.5 MN, about 65.3 MN in total; a factor of safety of 2.5 gives an allowable load of about 26.1 MN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每支沉箱鑽至岩盤後由大地工程師確認岩質與嵌岩長度，底部清潔度以目視或攝影檢查；澆置前檢查鋼筋籠與套管，澆置時記錄混凝土方量與理論方量比，偏差過大即檢討孔壁坍塌或擴孔。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each caisson reaches rock, the geotechnical engineer confirms rock quality and socket length and checks base cleanliness visually or by camera; reinforcement cages and casings are inspected before concreting, and the ratio of placed to theoretical concrete volume is logged, with large deviations prompting review for collapse or over-break.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"嵌岩沉箱 Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b。取 D = 3.05 m（10 ft）、嵌岩長 L_s = 3 m、側摩擦 f_s = 1.0 MPa、端承 q_b = 5 MPa：側摩擦 ≈ 28.7 MN、端承 ≈ 36.5 MN，合計約 65.3 MN；以安全係數 2.5 得容許約 26.1 MN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a rock-socketed caisson Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b. With D = 3.05 m (10 ft), a socket length L_s = 3 m, side friction f_s = 1.0 MPa and end bearing q_b = 5 MPa, side friction gives about 28.7 MN and end bearing about 36.5 MN, about 65.3 MN in total; a factor of safety of 2.5 gives an allowable load of about 26.1 MN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons\", which statement holds?","options":["在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。","嵌岩沉箱 Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b。","框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk.","For a rock-socketed caisson Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b.","All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"嵌岩沉箱 Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a rock-socketed caisson Q = πDL_sf_s + (πD²/4)q_b. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b028-v13-23","title":"深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岩盤嵌入沉箱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rock-socketed caissons” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每支沉箱鑽至岩盤後由大地工程師確認岩質與嵌岩長度，底部清潔度以目視或攝影檢查；澆置前檢查鋼筋籠與套管，澆置時記錄混凝土方量與理論方量比，偏差過大即檢討孔壁坍塌或擴孔。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each caisson reaches rock, the geotechnical engineer confirms rock quality and socket length and checks base cleanliness visually or by camera; reinforcement cages and casings are inspected before concreting, and the ratio of placed to theoretical concrete volume is logged, with large deviations prompting review for collapse or over-break. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：沉箱基底與嵌岩長度驗收列為停留點，每支沉箱都要有含照片與量測的竣工紀錄，作為日後改造時評估既有基礎容量的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make base and socket acceptance a hold point and keep an as-built record with photographs and measurements for every caisson, as the basis for evaluating existing foundation capacity in future alterations.","failure":"注意干擾：底部沉泥未清除會讓沉箱在加載後產生額外沉陷；黏土擠入或地下水湧入造成斷樁或夾泥，柱荷重集中到相鄰沉箱，使上部框管出現不均勻沉陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sediment left at the base causes extra settlement under load; clay squeezing or groundwater inflow creates necking or soil inclusions, shifting column load to neighbouring caissons and causing uneven settlement in the tubes above. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每支沉箱鑽至岩盤後由大地工程師確認岩質與嵌岩長度，底部清潔度以目視或攝影檢查；澆置前檢查鋼筋籠與套管，澆置時記錄混凝土方量與理論方量比，偏差過大即檢討孔壁坍塌或擴孔。","textEn":"After each caisson reaches rock, the geotechnical engineer confirms rock quality and socket length and checks base cleanliness visually or by camera; reinforcement cages and casings are inspected before concreting, and the ratio of placed to theoretical concrete volume is logged, with large deviations prompting review for collapse or over-break.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"沉箱基底與嵌岩長度驗收列為停留點，每支沉箱都要有含照片與量測的竣工紀錄，作為日後改造時評估既有基礎容量的依據。","textEn":"Make base and socket acceptance a hold point and keep an as-built record with photographs and measurements for every caisson, as the basis for evaluating existing foundation capacity in future alterations.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。","每支沉箱鑽至岩盤後由大地工程師確認岩質與嵌岩長度，底部清潔度以目視或攝影檢查。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters.","After each caisson reaches rock, the geotechnical engineer confirms rock quality and socket length and checks base cleanliness visually or by camera."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每支沉箱鑽至岩盤後由大地工程師確認岩質與嵌岩長度，底部清潔度以目視或攝影檢查；澆置前檢查鋼筋籠與套管，澆置時記錄混凝土方量與理論方量比，偏差過大即檢討孔壁坍塌或擴孔。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each caisson reaches rock, the geotechnical engineer confirms rock quality and socket length and checks base cleanliness visually or by camera; reinforcement cages and casings are inspected before concreting, and the ratio of placed to theoretical concrete volume is logged, with large deviations prompting review for collapse or over-break. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b028-v13-24","title":"深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岩盤嵌入沉箱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rock-socketed caissons” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"底部沉泥未清除會讓沉箱在加載後產生額外沉陷；黏土擠入或地下水湧入造成斷樁或夾泥，柱荷重集中到相鄰沉箱，使上部框管出現不均勻沉陷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sediment left at the base causes extra settlement under load; clay squeezing or groundwater inflow creates necking or soil inclusions, shifting column load to neighbouring caissons and causing uneven settlement in the tubes above. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：沉箱的承載包括嵌岩段的側摩擦與底部端承；施工時地下水與黏土擠入會影響孔壁穩定與底部清潔，所以鋼套管與底部檢查是品質的關鍵。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Capacity comes from side friction in the rock socket and end bearing at the base; during construction groundwater and squeezing clay threaten hole stability and base cleanliness, so steel casings and base inspection are key to quality.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"底部沉泥未清除會讓沉箱在加載後產生額外沉陷；黏土擠入或地下水湧入造成斷樁或夾泥，柱荷重集中到相鄰沉箱，使上部框管出現不均勻沉陷。","textEn":"Sediment left at the base causes extra settlement under load; clay squeezing or groundwater inflow creates necking or soil inclusions, shifting column load to neighbouring caissons and causing uneven settlement in the tubes above.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「深開挖與岩盤沉箱基礎」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deep excavation and rock-socketed caissons\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["底部沉泥未清除會讓沉箱在加載後產生額外沉陷；黏土擠入或地下水湧入造成斷樁或夾泥，柱荷重集中到相鄰沉箱，使上部框管出現不均勻沉陷。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。"],"optionsEn":["Sediment left at the base causes extra settlement under load.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"底部沉泥未清除會讓沉箱在加載後產生額外沉陷；黏土擠入或地下水湧入造成斷樁或夾泥，柱荷重集中到相鄰沉箱，使上部框管出現不均勻沉陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sediment left at the base causes extra settlement under load; clay squeezing or groundwater inflow creates necking or soil inclusions, shifting column load to neighbouring caissons and causing uneven settlement in the tubes above. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b028-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「經驗週期公式與實測比對」與「外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Empirical period formulas versus measurement\" and \"Skin insulation and column thermal movement\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b028-v13-25","title":"經驗週期公式與實測比對：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Empirical period formulas versus measurement: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「週期估算與環境振動」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Period estimates and ambient vibration” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"結構第一週期決定風致共振與地震反應的大小。規範的近似週期公式是為了訂定保守的基底剪力下限，主要由一般高度建築的實測統計得來，套用在超過 400 m 的超高層時只能當作量級檢查。實際週期取決於質量分布、框管勁度、收進與非結構構件，應以模態分析計算，並在完工後以環境振動量測校核；不同方向與扭轉模態要分開辨識，因為束筒在上部的不對稱會讓兩個水平方向的週期不同。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「週期估算與環境振動」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The first period controls wind resonance and seismic response. Code approximate-period formulas exist to set a conservative lower bound on base shear and come mainly from measurements of ordinary-height buildings, so for a tower above 400 m they are only an order-of-magnitude check. The real period depends on mass distribution, tube stiffness, setbacks and non-structural elements and should be computed by modal analysis and checked by ambient-vibration measurement after completion; each horizontal direction and the torsional mode must be identified separately, because the asymmetric upper bundle makes the two horizontal periods differ. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Period estimates and ambient vibration” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：ASCE 7 鋼抗彎框架近似週期 T_a = 0.0724h^0.8（h 以 m 計）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The ASCE 7 approximate period for steel moment frames is T_a = 0.0724h^0.8 with h in metres.","failure":"常見誤解：「規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「週期估算與環境振動」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Period estimates and ambient vibration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-25-k1","title":"經驗週期公式與實測比對","titleEn":"Empirical period formulas versus measurement","text":"結構第一週期決定風致共振與地震反應的大小。規範的近似週期公式是為了訂定保守的基底剪力下限，主要由一般高度建築的實測統計得來，套用在超過 400 m 的超高層時只能當作量級檢查。","textEn":"The first period controls wind resonance and seismic response. Code approximate-period formulas exist to set a conservative lower bound on base shear and come mainly from measurements of ordinary-height buildings, so for a tower above 400 m they are only an order-of-magnitude check.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「經驗週期公式與實測比對」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Empirical period formulas versus measurement\" is correct?","options":["規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。","結構第一週期決定風致共振與地震反應的大小。","帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。"],"optionsEn":["Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower.","The first period controls wind resonance and seismic response.","The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces."],"answer":1,"explanation":"結構第一週期決定風致共振與地震反應的大小。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The first period controls wind resonance and seismic response. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b028-v13-26","title":"經驗週期公式與實測比對：定量估算","titleEn":"Empirical period formulas versus measurement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「週期估算與環境振動」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Period estimates and ambient vibration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：ASCE 7 鋼抗彎框架近似週期 T_a = 0.0724h^0.8（h 以 m 計）。h = 442.1 m 時 T_a = 0.0724×442.1^0.8 ≈ 9.47 s；常用的 T ≈ 0.1N 規則則得 0.1×108 = 10.8 s。兩者相差約 14%，說明經驗式只能當量級參考，設計須以模態分析為準。數值為教學比較。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The ASCE 7 approximate period for steel moment frames is T_a = 0.0724h^0.8 with h in metres. For h = 442.1 m, T_a = 0.0724×442.1^0.8 ≈ 9.47 s, while the common rule T ≈ 0.1N gives 0.1×108 = 10.8 s. The 14% gap shows that empirical formulas are only order-of-magnitude references and design must rely on modal analysis. Values are a teaching comparison. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在頂部與中段設置雙向加速度計，於低風時段記錄至少一小時的環境振動，以頻域分解辨識兩個水平方向與扭轉的前幾個模態，並與模態分析比較；差異超過約一成時檢討質量與勁度假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Install biaxial accelerometers at the top and mid-height, record at least an hour of ambient vibration in calm conditions, identify the first modes in both horizontal directions and torsion by frequency-domain decomposition, and compare with modal analysis; review mass and stiffness assumptions if the difference exceeds about ten percent.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"ASCE 7 鋼抗彎框架近似週期 T_a = 0.0724h^0.8（h 以 m 計）。h = 442.1 m 時 T_a = 0.0724×442.1^0.8 ≈ 9.47 s；常用的 T ≈ 0.1N 規則則得 0.1×108 = 10.8 s。兩者相差約 14%，說明經驗式只能當量級參考，設計須以模態分析為準。數值為教學比較。","textEn":"The ASCE 7 approximate period for steel moment frames is T_a = 0.0724h^0.8 with h in metres. For h = 442.1 m, T_a = 0.0724×442.1^0.8 ≈ 9.47 s, while the common rule T ≈ 0.1N gives 0.1×108 = 10.8 s. The 14% gap shows that empirical formulas are only order-of-magnitude references and design must rely on modal analysis. Values are a teaching comparison.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「經驗週期公式與實測比對」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Empirical period formulas versus measurement\", which statement holds?","options":["裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。","收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。","ASCE 7 鋼抗彎框架近似週期 T_a = 0.0724h^0.8（h 以 m 計）。"],"optionsEn":["Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity.","Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour.","The ASCE 7 approximate period for steel moment frames is T_a = 0.0724h^0.8 with h in metres."],"answer":2,"explanation":"ASCE 7 鋼抗彎框架近似週期 T_a = 0.0724h^0.8（h 以 m 計）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The ASCE 7 approximate period for steel moment frames is T_a = 0.0724h^0.8 with h in metres. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b028-v13-27","title":"經驗週期公式與實測比對：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Empirical period formulas versus measurement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「週期估算與環境振動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Period estimates and ambient vibration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在頂部與中段設置雙向加速度計，於低風時段記錄至少一小時的環境振動，以頻域分解辨識兩個水平方向與扭轉的前幾個模態，並與模態分析比較；差異超過約一成時檢討質量與勁度假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Install biaxial accelerometers at the top and mid-height, record at least an hour of ambient vibration in calm conditions, identify the first modes in both horizontal directions and torsion by frequency-domain decomposition, and compare with modal analysis; review mass and stiffness assumptions if the difference exceeds about ten percent. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計報告應同時列出經驗週期、模態分析週期與（若有）實測週期，並說明採用哪一個做為風與地震設計依據；改造或增減大量質量後，要重新量測並更新紀錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design reports should list the empirical, modal-analysis and any measured periods and state which governs wind and seismic design; after renovations that add or remove large masses, measure again and update the record.","failure":"注意干擾：若直接用經驗週期推算風致共振或阻尼需求，可能錯估臨界風速與加速度；忽略兩方向週期不同，則可能把兩個相近的模態誤判為一個，低估扭轉耦合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using an empirical period to estimate wind resonance or damping needs can misjudge critical wind speed and acceleration; ignoring the different periods in the two directions can merge two close modes into one and underestimate torsional coupling. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在頂部與中段設置雙向加速度計，於低風時段記錄至少一小時的環境振動，以頻域分解辨識兩個水平方向與扭轉的前幾個模態，並與模態分析比較；差異超過約一成時檢討質量與勁度假設。","textEn":"Install biaxial accelerometers at the top and mid-height, record at least an hour of ambient vibration in calm conditions, identify the first modes in both horizontal directions and torsion by frequency-domain decomposition, and compare with modal analysis; review mass and stiffness assumptions if the difference exceeds about ten percent.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計報告應同時列出經驗週期、模態分析週期與（若有）實測週期，並說明採用哪一個做為風與地震設計依據；改造或增減大量質量後，要重新量測並更新紀錄。","textEn":"Design reports should list the empirical, modal-analysis and any measured periods and state which governs wind and seismic design; after renovations that add or remove large masses, measure again and update the record.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「經驗週期公式與實測比對」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Empirical period formulas versus measurement\"?","options":["在頂部與中段設置雙向加速度計，於低風時段記錄至少一小時的環境振動，以頻域分解辨識兩個水平方向與扭轉的前幾個模態，並與模態分析比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。"],"optionsEn":["Install biaxial accelerometers at the top and mid-height, record at least an hour of ambient vibration in calm conditions, identify the first modes in both horizontal directions and torsion by frequency-domain decomposition, and compare with modal analysis.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在頂部與中段設置雙向加速度計，於低風時段記錄至少一小時的環境振動，以頻域分解辨識兩個水平方向與扭轉的前幾個模態，並與模態分析比較；差異超過約一成時檢討質量與勁度假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Install biaxial accelerometers at the top and mid-height, record at least an hour of ambient vibration in calm conditions, identify the first modes in both horizontal directions and torsion by frequency-domain decomposition, and compare with modal analysis; review mass and stiffness assumptions if the difference exceeds about ten percent. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b028-v13-28","title":"經驗週期公式與實測比對：失效診斷","titleEn":"Empirical period formulas versus measurement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「週期估算與環境振動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Period estimates and ambient vibration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若直接用經驗週期推算風致共振或阻尼需求，可能錯估臨界風速與加速度；忽略兩方向週期不同，則可能把兩個相近的模態誤判為一個，低估扭轉耦合。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using an empirical period to estimate wind resonance or damping needs can misjudge critical wind speed and acceleration; ignoring the different periods in the two directions can merge two close modes into one and underestimate torsional coupling. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：實際週期取決於質量分布、框管勁度、收進與非結構構件，應以模態分析計算，並在完工後以環境振動量測校核；不同方向與扭轉模態要分開辨識，因為束筒在上部的不對稱會讓兩個水平方向的週期不同。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The real period depends on mass distribution, tube stiffness, setbacks and non-structural elements and should be computed by modal analysis and checked by ambient-vibration measurement after completion; each horizontal direction and the torsional mode must be identified separately, because the asymmetric upper bundle makes the two horizontal periods differ.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若直接用經驗週期推算風致共振或阻尼需求，可能錯估臨界風速與加速度；忽略兩方向週期不同，則可能把兩個相近的模態誤判為一個，低估扭轉耦合。","textEn":"Using an empirical period to estimate wind resonance or damping needs can misjudge critical wind speed and acceleration; ignoring the different periods in the two directions can merge two close modes into one and underestimate torsional coupling.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「經驗週期公式與實測比對」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Empirical period formulas versus measurement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若直接用經驗週期推算風致共振或阻尼需求，可能錯估臨界風速與加速度；忽略兩方向週期不同，則可能把兩個相近的模態誤判為一個，低估扭轉耦合。","帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using an empirical period to estimate wind resonance or damping needs can misjudge critical wind speed and acceleration.","The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若直接用經驗週期推算風致共振或阻尼需求，可能錯估臨界風速與加速度；忽略兩方向週期不同，則可能把兩個相近的模態誤判為一個，低估扭轉耦合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using an empirical period to estimate wind resonance or damping needs can misjudge critical wind speed and acceleration; ignoring the different periods in the two directions can merge two close modes into one and underestimate torsional coupling. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b028-v13-29","title":"外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Skin insulation and column thermal movement: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「外牆熱隔離與柱溫差」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Skin thermal isolation and column temperature” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"SOM 說明黑色鋁皮與青銅色玻璃外牆把結構與室外隔開，使鋼構溫度相對穩定，減少框架的熱脹冷縮。芝加哥冬夏溫差大，若周邊柱直接暴露，外柱與恆溫室內的內部柱會產生顯著溫差，數百公尺高的柱列累積的長度差會讓上部樓板傾斜、隔間開裂並在樓板梁中產生附加力。外牆保溫與柱的防火被覆共同決定實際溫差，因此外牆改造時也要回頭檢核結構。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外牆熱隔離與柱溫差」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"SOM explains that the black aluminium and bronze-tinted glass skin isolates the structure from outside temperature, keeping the steel relatively stable and limiting expansion and contraction of the frame. Chicago has large seasonal temperature swings; if perimeter columns were exposed, the difference between outer columns and interior columns in conditioned space would accumulate over hundreds of metres into length differences that tilt upper floors, crack partitions and induce forces in floor beams. Skin insulation and column fireproofing together set the actual temperature difference, so façade renovations must also be checked structurally. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Skin thermal isolation and column temperature” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：柱長差 ΔL = αLΔT。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Column length difference ΔL = αLΔT.","failure":"常見誤解：「帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外牆熱隔離與柱溫差」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Skin thermal isolation and column temperature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-29-k1","title":"外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形","titleEn":"Skin insulation and column thermal movement","text":"SOM 說明黑色鋁皮與青銅色玻璃外牆把結構與室外隔開，使鋼構溫度相對穩定，減少框架的熱脹冷縮。芝加哥冬夏溫差大，若周邊柱直接暴露，外柱與恆溫室內的內部柱會產生顯著溫差，數百公尺高的柱列累積的長度差會讓上部樓板傾斜、隔間開裂並在樓板梁中產生附加力。","textEn":"SOM explains that the black aluminium and bronze-tinted glass skin isolates the structure from outside temperature, keeping the steel relatively stable and limiting expansion and contraction of the frame. Chicago has large seasonal temperature swings; if perimeter columns were exposed, the difference between outer columns and interior columns in conditioned space would accumulate over hundreds of metres into length differences that tilt upper floors, crack partitions and induce forces in floor beams.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Skin insulation and column thermal movement\" is correct?","options":["帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。","在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。","SOM 說明黑色鋁皮與青銅色玻璃外牆把結構與室外隔開，使鋼構溫度相對穩定，減少框架的熱脹冷縮。"],"optionsEn":["The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces.","Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk.","SOM explains that the black aluminium and bronze-tinted glass skin isolates the structure from outside temperature, keeping the steel relatively stable and limiting expansion and contraction of the frame."],"answer":2,"explanation":"SOM 說明黑色鋁皮與青銅色玻璃外牆把結構與室外隔開，使鋼構溫度相對穩定，減少框架的熱脹冷縮。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"SOM explains that the black aluminium and bronze-tinted glass skin isolates the structure from outside temperature, keeping the steel relatively stable and limiting expansion and contraction of the frame. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b028-v13-30","title":"外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形：定量估算","titleEn":"Skin insulation and column thermal movement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外牆熱隔離與柱溫差」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Skin thermal isolation and column temperature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：柱長差 ΔL = αLΔT。L = 400 m、α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C：外柱與內柱溫差 30 °C 時 ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×400,000×30 = 144 mm；外牆隔熱把溫差降到 5 °C 時 ΔL = 24 mm。若外柱到最近內柱距離 9 m，樓板坡度由 144/9,000 ≈ 1/63 降到 24/9,000 ≈ 1/375。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Column length difference ΔL = αLΔT. For L = 400 m and α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C, a 30 °C difference between outer and inner columns gives ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×400,000×30 = 144 mm; insulating the skin to cut the difference to 5 °C gives ΔL = 24 mm. Over 9 m to the nearest interior column the floor slope falls from 144/9,000 ≈ 1/63 to 24/9,000 ≈ 1/375. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在代表性外柱與內柱裝設溫度感測器，冬季與夏季各記錄數週，並在頂部樓層以精密水準量測外柱與內柱的相對高程變化，與溫差換算值比較；外牆維修時抽查保溫層連續性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Install temperature sensors on representative exterior and interior columns, record for several weeks in winter and summer, and use precise levelling at upper floors to measure relative elevation changes between exterior and interior columns, comparing them with values computed from the temperature difference; spot-check insulation continuity during façade maintenance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"柱長差 ΔL = αLΔT。L = 400 m、α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C：外柱與內柱溫差 30 °C 時 ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×400,000×30 = 144 mm；外牆隔熱把溫差降到 5 °C 時 ΔL = 24 mm。若外柱到最近內柱距離 9 m，樓板坡度由 144/9,000 ≈ 1/63 降到 24/9,000 ≈ 1/375。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Column length difference ΔL = αLΔT. For L = 400 m and α = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C, a 30 °C difference between outer and inner columns gives ΔL = 12×10⁻⁶×400,000×30 = 144 mm; insulating the skin to cut the difference to 5 °C gives ΔL = 24 mm. Over 9 m to the nearest interior column the floor slope falls from 144/9,000 ≈ 1/63 to 24/9,000 ≈ 1/375. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Skin insulation and column thermal movement\", which statement holds?","options":["柱長差 ΔL = αLΔT。","框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。","框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。"],"optionsEn":["Column length difference ΔL = αLΔT.","All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally.","A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters."],"answer":0,"explanation":"柱長差 ΔL = αLΔT。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Column length difference ΔL = αLΔT. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b028-v13-31","title":"外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Skin insulation and column thermal movement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外牆熱隔離與柱溫差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Skin thermal isolation and column temperature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在代表性外柱與內柱裝設溫度感測器，冬季與夏季各記錄數週，並在頂部樓層以精密水準量測外柱與內柱的相對高程變化，與溫差換算值比較；外牆維修時抽查保溫層連續性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Install temperature sensors on representative exterior and interior columns, record for several weeks in winter and summer, and use precise levelling at upper floors to measure relative elevation changes between exterior and interior columns, comparing them with values computed from the temperature difference; spot-check insulation continuity during façade maintenance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：外牆或節能改造的設計審查清單應包含柱溫度條件的變化評估，並由結構工程師簽認；交接文件中保留原設計採用的柱溫差假設。","observationEn":"Site practice: The design review checklist for façade or energy retrofits should include an assessment of changed column temperature conditions signed by the structural engineer, and handover documents should keep the original design assumption for column temperature difference.","failure":"注意干擾：外牆改造時若拆除保溫或改用大面積透明玻璃而未評估柱溫差，上部樓板可能出現季節性傾斜、隔間與門框開裂，連接外柱與內部構件的梁端也會承受反覆溫度應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Removing insulation or switching to large clear glazing during a façade renovation without assessing column temperatures can cause seasonal floor tilt, cracked partitions and door frames, and cyclic thermal stresses at beam ends linking exterior and interior members. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在代表性外柱與內柱裝設溫度感測器，冬季與夏季各記錄數週，並在頂部樓層以精密水準量測外柱與內柱的相對高程變化，與溫差換算值比較；外牆維修時抽查保溫層連續性。","textEn":"Install temperature sensors on representative exterior and interior columns, record for several weeks in winter and summer, and use precise levelling at upper floors to measure relative elevation changes between exterior and interior columns, comparing them with values computed from the temperature difference; spot-check insulation continuity during façade maintenance.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"外牆或節能改造的設計審查清單應包含柱溫度條件的變化評估，並由結構工程師簽認；交接文件中保留原設計採用的柱溫差假設。","textEn":"The design review checklist for façade or energy retrofits should include an assessment of changed column temperature conditions signed by the structural engineer, and handover documents should keep the original design assumption for column temperature difference.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Skin insulation and column thermal movement\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在代表性外柱與內柱裝設溫度感測器，冬季與夏季各記錄數週，並在頂部樓層以精密水準量測外柱與內柱的相對高程變化，與溫差換算值比較；外牆維修時抽查保溫層連續性。","鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Install temperature sensors on representative exterior and interior columns, record for several weeks in winter and summer, and use precise levelling at upper floors to measure relative elevation changes between exterior and interior columns, comparing them with values computed from the temperature difference.","Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在代表性外柱與內柱裝設溫度感測器，冬季與夏季各記錄數週，並在頂部樓層以精密水準量測外柱與內柱的相對高程變化，與溫差換算值比較；外牆維修時抽查保溫層連續性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Install temperature sensors on representative exterior and interior columns, record for several weeks in winter and summer, and use precise levelling at upper floors to measure relative elevation changes between exterior and interior columns, comparing them with values computed from the temperature difference; spot-check insulation continuity during façade maintenance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b028-v13-32","title":"外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Skin insulation and column thermal movement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外牆熱隔離與柱溫差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Skin thermal isolation and column temperature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"外牆改造時若拆除保溫或改用大面積透明玻璃而未評估柱溫差，上部樓板可能出現季節性傾斜、隔間與門框開裂，連接外柱與內部構件的梁端也會承受反覆溫度應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Removing insulation or switching to large clear glazing during a façade renovation without assessing column temperatures can cause seasonal floor tilt, cracked partitions and door frames, and cyclic thermal stresses at beam ends linking exterior and interior members. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：外牆保溫與柱的防火被覆共同決定實際溫差，因此外牆改造時也要回頭檢核結構。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Skin insulation and column fireproofing together set the actual temperature difference, so façade renovations must also be checked structurally.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「帷幕牆只負責防水與外觀，與主結構的受力無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The curtain wall is only for weather-tightness and appearance and has nothing to do with structural forces.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"外牆改造時若拆除保溫或改用大面積透明玻璃而未評估柱溫差，上部樓板可能出現季節性傾斜、隔間與門框開裂，連接外柱與內部構件的梁端也會承受反覆溫度應力。","textEn":"Removing insulation or switching to large clear glazing during a façade renovation without assessing column temperatures can cause seasonal floor tilt, cracked partitions and door frames, and cyclic thermal stresses at beam ends linking exterior and interior members.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外牆隔熱與柱溫差變形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Skin insulation and column thermal movement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。","外牆改造時若拆除保溫或改用大面積透明玻璃而未評估柱溫差，上部樓板可能出現季節性傾斜、隔間與門框開裂，連接外柱與內部構件的梁端也會承受反覆溫度應力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk.","Removing insulation or switching to large clear glazing during a façade renovation without assessing column temperatures can cause seasonal floor tilt, cracked partitions and door frames, and cyclic thermal stresses at beam ends linking exterior and interior members."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外牆改造時若拆除保溫或改用大面積透明玻璃而未評估柱溫差，上部樓板可能出現季節性傾斜、隔間與門框開裂，連接外柱與內部構件的梁端也會承受反覆溫度應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Removing insulation or switching to large clear glazing during a façade renovation without assessing column temperatures can cause seasonal floor tilt, cracked partitions and door frames, and cyclic thermal stresses at beam ends linking exterior and interior members. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b028-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「營運中改造的柱補強」與「改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation\" and \"Tube load path and records during alteration\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b028-v13-33","title":"營運中改造的柱補強：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「既有柱的包覆補強」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Encasement strengthening of existing columns” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"2017 年起的底座改造在原廣場位置加建三層商業裙樓，約 20 根下層廣場鋼柱無法直接承受增加的樓層。可行處以焊接頭剪力釘於腹板後包覆混凝土，讓鋼柱與混凝土共同受壓；無法包覆處則在翼板焊上局部長度的補強板，並以分段（階梯式）構件檢核補強與未補強斷面。改造全程大樓持續營運，施工順序、臨時支撐與既有基礎容量都必須逐步確認。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「既有柱的包覆補強」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"From 2017 the base repositioning added a three-storey retail podium on the former plaza, and about 20 lower-level plaza columns could not carry the added floors as they were. Where possible, headed studs were welded to the column webs and the columns encased in concrete so steel and concrete share compression; where encasement was impossible, partial-length plates were welded to the flanges and the columns checked as stepped members with reinforced and unreinforced sections. The tower stayed open throughout, so sequencing, temporary support and existing foundation capacity had to be confirmed step by step. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Encasement strengthening of existing columns” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：包覆後軸壓強度 P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Encased squash capacity is P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c.","failure":"常見誤解：「在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「既有柱的包覆補強」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Encasement strengthening of existing columns”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-33-k1","title":"營運中改造的柱補強","titleEn":"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation","text":"2017 年起的底座改造在原廣場位置加建三層商業裙樓，約 20 根下層廣場鋼柱無法直接承受增加的樓層。可行處以焊接頭剪力釘於腹板後包覆混凝土，讓鋼柱與混凝土共同受壓；無法包覆處則在翼板焊上局部長度的補強板，並以分段（階梯式）構件檢核補強與未補強斷面。","textEn":"From 2017 the base repositioning added a three-storey retail podium on the former plaza, and about 20 lower-level plaza columns could not carry the added floors as they were. Where possible, headed studs were welded to the column webs and the columns encased in concrete so steel and concrete share compression; where encasement was impossible, partial-length plates were welded to the flanges and the columns checked as stepped members with reinforced and unreinforced sections.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「營運中改造的柱補強」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation\" is correct?","options":["2017 年起的底座改造在原廣場位置加建三層商業裙樓，約 20 根下層廣場鋼柱無法直接承受增加的樓層。","在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。","裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。"],"optionsEn":["From 2017 the base repositioning added a three-storey retail podium on the former plaza, and about 20 lower-level plaza columns could not carry the added floors as they were.","Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk.","Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"2017 年起的底座改造在原廣場位置加建三層商業裙樓，約 20 根下層廣場鋼柱無法直接承受增加的樓層。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"From 2017 the base repositioning added a three-storey retail podium on the former plaza, and about 20 lower-level plaza columns could not carry the added floors as they were. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b028-v13-34","title":"營運中改造的柱補強：定量估算","titleEn":"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「既有柱的包覆補強」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Encasement strengthening of existing columns” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：包覆後軸壓強度 P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c。既有鋼柱 A_s = 0.0258 m²、F_y = 345 MPa，P_s ≈ 8.90 MN；包覆 0.6 m×0.6 m、f′c = 35 MPa，A_c = 0.36 − 0.0258 = 0.334 m²，混凝土貢獻 ≈ 0.85×35×0.334 ≈ 9.94 MN，合計約 18.8 MN，約為原鋼柱的 2.1 倍（未計長細比折減）。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Encased squash capacity is P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c. An existing column with A_s = 0.0258 m² and F_y = 345 MPa gives P_s ≈ 8.90 MN; a 0.6 m×0.6 m encasement with f′c = 35 MPa has A_c = 0.36 − 0.0258 = 0.334 m² and adds about 0.85×35×0.334 ≈ 9.94 MN, about 18.8 MN in total, roughly 2.1 times the bare steel column before slenderness reduction. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：補強前以現場量測確認既有柱斷面與鋼材等級（必要時取樣試驗），剪力釘焊接做彎曲試驗抽驗，翼板補強焊道做磁粒或超音波檢測；新增荷載分階段施加時量測柱應變與基礎沉陷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before strengthening, confirm existing column sections and steel grade by survey, with coupon testing if needed; bend-test a sample of welded studs and inspect flange-plate welds by magnetic-particle or ultrasonic testing; measure column strain and foundation settlement as new loads are applied in stages.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"包覆後軸壓強度 P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c。既有鋼柱 A_s = 0.0258 m²、F_y = 345 MPa，P_s ≈ 8.90 MN；包覆 0.6 m×0.6 m、f′c = 35 MPa，A_c = 0.36 − 0.0258 = 0.334 m²，混凝土貢獻 ≈ 0.85×35×0.334 ≈ 9.94 MN，合計約 18.8 MN，約為原鋼柱的 2.1 倍（未計長細比折減）。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Encased squash capacity is P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c. An existing column with A_s = 0.0258 m² and F_y = 345 MPa gives P_s ≈ 8.90 MN; a 0.6 m×0.6 m encasement with f′c = 35 MPa has A_c = 0.36 − 0.0258 = 0.334 m² and adds about 0.85×35×0.334 ≈ 9.94 MN, about 18.8 MN in total, roughly 2.1 times the bare steel column before slenderness reduction. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「營運中改造的柱補強」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation\", which statement holds?","options":["收進只是為了造型與出租面積，對結構行為沒有影響。","包覆後軸壓強度 P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c。","樓板桁架只要強度足夠，剪力釘可以減量而不影響行為。"],"optionsEn":["Setbacks serve only appearance and leasing and do not affect structural behaviour.","Encased squash capacity is P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c.","If the floor trusses are strong enough, shear studs can be reduced without affecting behaviour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"包覆後軸壓強度 P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Encased squash capacity is P = A_sF_y + 0.85f′cA_c. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b028-v13-35","title":"營運中改造的柱補強：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「既有柱的包覆補強」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Encasement strengthening of existing columns” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"補強前以現場量測確認既有柱斷面與鋼材等級（必要時取樣試驗），剪力釘焊接做彎曲試驗抽驗，翼板補強焊道做磁粒或超音波檢測；新增荷載分階段施加時量測柱應變與基礎沉陷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before strengthening, confirm existing column sections and steel grade by survey, with coupon testing if needed; bend-test a sample of welded studs and inspect flange-plate welds by magnetic-particle or ultrasonic testing; measure column strain and foundation settlement as new loads are applied in stages. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對承載中構件的焊接須有專門的焊接程序與熱輸入限制、必要的臨時卸載或支撐，並把「包覆混凝土達到規定強度」列為施加新增荷載前的停留點，由結構工程師簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Welding on loaded members requires a dedicated procedure with heat-input limits and temporary unloading or shoring where needed, and the encasement reaching its specified strength must be a hold point before new loads are applied, signed off by the structural engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：在承載中的柱上焊接補強板，若熱輸入過大會使局部鋼材在高應力下軟化與變形；包覆混凝土若在新增荷載之前未達強度，荷載仍全部由鋼柱承受，補強效果打折扣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Welding plates onto a loaded column with excessive heat input can soften and distort the steel locally under high stress; if the encasement has not gained strength before new load arrives, the steel still carries it all and the strengthening is compromised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"補強前以現場量測確認既有柱斷面與鋼材等級（必要時取樣試驗），剪力釘焊接做彎曲試驗抽驗，翼板補強焊道做磁粒或超音波檢測；新增荷載分階段施加時量測柱應變與基礎沉陷。","textEn":"Before strengthening, confirm existing column sections and steel grade by survey, with coupon testing if needed; bend-test a sample of welded studs and inspect flange-plate welds by magnetic-particle or ultrasonic testing; measure column strain and foundation settlement as new loads are applied in stages.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對承載中構件的焊接須有專門的焊接程序與熱輸入限制、必要的臨時卸載或支撐，並把「包覆混凝土達到規定強度」列為施加新增荷載前的停留點，由結構工程師簽認。","textEn":"Welding on loaded members requires a dedicated procedure with heat-input limits and temporary unloading or shoring where needed, and the encasement reaching its specified strength must be a hold point before new loads are applied, signed off by the structural engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「營運中改造的柱補強」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","沉箱只要鑽到岩盤表面就能發揮全部承載力。","補強前以現場量測確認既有柱斷面與鋼材等級（必要時取樣試驗），剪力釘焊接做彎曲試驗抽驗，翼板補強焊道做磁粒或超音波檢測；新增荷載分階段施加時量測柱應變與基礎沉陷。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A caisson develops full capacity as soon as it touches the rock surface.","Before strengthening, confirm existing column sections and steel grade by survey, with coupon testing if needed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"補強前以現場量測確認既有柱斷面與鋼材等級（必要時取樣試驗），剪力釘焊接做彎曲試驗抽驗，翼板補強焊道做磁粒或超音波檢測；新增荷載分階段施加時量測柱應變與基礎沉陷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before strengthening, confirm existing column sections and steel grade by survey, with coupon testing if needed; bend-test a sample of welded studs and inspect flange-plate welds by magnetic-particle or ultrasonic testing; measure column strain and foundation settlement as new loads are applied in stages. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b028-v13-36","title":"營運中改造的柱補強：失效診斷","titleEn":"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「既有柱的包覆補強」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Encasement strengthening of existing columns” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在承載中的柱上焊接補強板，若熱輸入過大會使局部鋼材在高應力下軟化與變形；包覆混凝土若在新增荷載之前未達強度，荷載仍全部由鋼柱承受，補強效果打折扣。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Welding plates onto a loaded column with excessive heat input can soften and distort the steel locally under high stress; if the encasement has not gained strength before new load arrives, the steel still carries it all and the strengthening is compromised. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：改造全程大樓持續營運，施工順序、臨時支撐與既有基礎容量都必須逐步確認。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The tower stayed open throughout, so sequencing, temporary support and existing foundation capacity had to be confirmed step by step.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「在承載中的鋼柱上焊接補強是沒有風險的例行作業。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Welding reinforcement onto a loaded steel column is a routine task with no risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在承載中的柱上焊接補強板，若熱輸入過大會使局部鋼材在高應力下軟化與變形；包覆混凝土若在新增荷載之前未達強度，荷載仍全部由鋼柱承受，補強效果打折扣。","textEn":"Welding plates onto a loaded column with excessive heat input can soften and distort the steel locally under high stress; if the encasement has not gained strength before new load arrives, the steel still carries it all and the strengthening is compromised.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「營運中改造的柱補強」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Column strengthening during an occupied renovation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["在承載中的柱上焊接補強板，若熱輸入過大會使局部鋼材在高應力下軟化與變形；包覆混凝土若在新增荷載之前未達強度，荷載仍全部由鋼柱承受，補強效果打折扣。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。"],"optionsEn":["Welding plates onto a loaded column with excessive heat input can soften and distort the steel locally under high stress.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在承載中的柱上焊接補強板，若熱輸入過大會使局部鋼材在高應力下軟化與變形；包覆混凝土若在新增荷載之前未達強度，荷載仍全部由鋼柱承受，補強效果打折扣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Welding plates onto a loaded column with excessive heat input can soften and distort the steel locally under high stress; if the encasement has not gained strength before new load arrives, the steel still carries it all and the strengthening is compromised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b028-v13-37","title":"改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Tube load path and records during alteration: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「入口裙梁更換與柱無側撐長度」如何影響威利斯大樓的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Entrance spandrel replacement and column bracing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Willis Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"改造時為了新設由街道到二樓的樓梯，三根 42 in 深的組合裙梁與樓梯衝突而被降低、拆除並以新的組合鋼板梁取代。公開資料指出這中斷了框管的傳力路徑，因此在相鄰的 110 層通高巨柱上加設局部補強，並依三維塔樓模型訂定拆除與替換順序。裙梁不只抵抗側力，也為柱提供側向支撐；拆除後柱的無側撐長度變長，受壓挫屈強度隨之下降，必須在替換完成前以臨時支撐補足。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「入口裙梁更換與柱無側撐長度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"To create a new stair from the street to level two, three 42 in deep built-up spandrels that clashed with it were lowered, removed and replaced with new built-up plate girders. Public sources note that this interrupted the tube's load path, so local reinforcing was added to the adjacent full-height columns, and the demolition and replacement sequence followed a three-dimensional tower model. Spandrels do not only resist lateral load; they also brace the columns, so removing them lengthens the unbraced length and reduces buckling strength, which must be made up with temporary bracing until replacement is complete. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Entrance spandrel replacement and column bracing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：AISC 柱強度：A = 0.0488 m²、I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴、F_y = 345 MPa、P_y ≈ 16,840 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: AISC column strength with A = 0.0488 m², I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴ and F_y = 345 MPa gives P_y ≈ 16,840 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「入口裙梁更換與柱無側撐長度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Entrance spandrel replacement and column bracing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-37-k1","title":"改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄","titleEn":"Tube load path and records during alteration","text":"改造時為了新設由街道到二樓的樓梯，三根 42 in 深的組合裙梁與樓梯衝突而被降低、拆除並以新的組合鋼板梁取代。公開資料指出這中斷了框管的傳力路徑，因此在相鄰的 110 層通高巨柱上加設局部補強，並依三維塔樓模型訂定拆除與替換順序。","textEn":"To create a new stair from the street to level two, three 42 in deep built-up spandrels that clashed with it were lowered, removed and replaced with new built-up plate girders. Public sources note that this interrupted the tube's load path, so local reinforcing was added to the adjacent full-height columns, and the demolition and replacement sequence followed a three-dimensional tower model.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tube load path and records during alteration\" is correct?","options":["裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。","改造時為了新設由街道到二樓的樓梯，三根 42 in 深的組合裙梁與樓梯衝突而被降低、拆除並以新的組合鋼板梁取代。","框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity.","To create a new stair from the street to level two, three 42 in deep built-up spandrels that clashed with it were lowered, removed and replaced with new built-up plate girders.","All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"改造時為了新設由街道到二樓的樓梯，三根 42 in 深的組合裙梁與樓梯衝突而被降低、拆除並以新的組合鋼板梁取代。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"To create a new stair from the street to level two, three 42 in deep built-up spandrels that clashed with it were lowered, removed and replaced with new built-up plate girders. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b028-v13-38","title":"改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄：定量估算","titleEn":"Tube load path and records during alteration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口裙梁更換與柱無側撐長度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Entrance spandrel replacement and column bracing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：AISC 柱強度：A = 0.0488 m²、I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴、F_y = 345 MPa、P_y ≈ 16,840 kN。無側撐長 3.91 m 時 P_e ≈ 69,300 kN，P_y/P_e ≈ 0.243，P_n = 0.658^0.243×P_y ≈ 15,200 kN；裙梁拆除使長度變 7.82 m，P_e ≈ 17,300 kN，P_y/P_e ≈ 0.971，P_n ≈ 11,200 kN，下降約 26%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: AISC column strength with A = 0.0488 m², I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴ and F_y = 345 MPa gives P_y ≈ 16,840 kN. At a 3.91 m unbraced length P_e ≈ 69,300 kN, P_y/P_e ≈ 0.243 and P_n = 0.658^0.243×P_y ≈ 15,200 kN; removing a spandrel doubles the length to 7.82 m, P_e ≈ 17,300 kN, P_y/P_e ≈ 0.971 and P_n ≈ 11,200 kN, about 26% less. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：拆除前以三維模型檢核每個拆除步驟的柱與相鄰構件需求容量比，臨時支撐安裝並驗收後才可切割；施工期間量測相鄰柱應變與垂直度，新裙梁接合完成並檢驗後才拆除臨時支撐，最後更新竣工圖與結構模型。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before demolition, check demand-to-capacity ratios of columns and adjacent members for every removal step in the three-dimensional model, and cut only after temporary bracing is installed and accepted; during the work monitor strain and plumbness of adjacent columns, remove temporary bracing only after the new spandrel connections are completed and inspected, then update the as-built drawings and structural model.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"AISC 柱強度：A = 0.0488 m²、I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴、F_y = 345 MPa、P_y ≈ 16,840 kN。無側撐長 3.91 m 時 P_e ≈ 69,300 kN，P_y/P_e ≈ 0.243，P_n = 0.658^0.243×P_y ≈ 15,200 kN；裙梁拆除使長度變 7.82 m，P_e ≈ 17,300 kN，P_y/P_e ≈ 0.971，P_n ≈ 11,200 kN，下降約 26%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"AISC column strength with A = 0.0488 m², I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴ and F_y = 345 MPa gives P_y ≈ 16,840 kN. At a 3.91 m unbraced length P_e ≈ 69,300 kN, P_y/P_e ≈ 0.243 and P_n = 0.658^0.243×P_y ≈ 15,200 kN; removing a spandrel doubles the length to 7.82 m, P_e ≈ 17,300 kN, P_y/P_e ≈ 0.971 and P_n ≈ 11,200 kN, about 26% less. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tube load path and records during alteration\", which statement holds?","options":["框管的側向勁度主要由柱子決定，裙梁大小影響不大。","鋼構安裝速度只取決於塔吊數量與工人數量。","AISC 柱強度：A = 0.0488 m²、I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴、F_y = 345 MPa、P_y ≈ 16,840 kN。"],"optionsEn":["A framed tube's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the columns; spandrel size hardly matters.","Steel erection speed depends only on the number of cranes and workers.","AISC column strength with A = 0.0488 m², I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴ and F_y = 345 MPa gives P_y ≈ 16,840 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"AISC 柱強度：A = 0.0488 m²、I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴、F_y = 345 MPa、P_y ≈ 16,840 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"AISC column strength with A = 0.0488 m², I = 5.37×10⁻⁴ m⁴ and F_y = 345 MPa gives P_y ≈ 16,840 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b028-v13-39","title":"改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tube load path and records during alteration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口裙梁更換與柱無側撐長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Entrance spandrel replacement and column bracing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"拆除前以三維模型檢核每個拆除步驟的柱與相鄰構件需求容量比，臨時支撐安裝並驗收後才可切割；施工期間量測相鄰柱應變與垂直度，新裙梁接合完成並檢驗後才拆除臨時支撐，最後更新竣工圖與結構模型。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before demolition, check demand-to-capacity ratios of columns and adjacent members for every removal step in the three-dimensional model, and cut only after temporary bracing is installed and accepted; during the work monitor strain and plumbness of adjacent columns, remove temporary bracing only after the new spandrel connections are completed and inspected, then update the as-built drawings and structural model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：營運中大樓的結構拆除必須有逐步的施工階段分析與臨時支撐計畫，切割作業列為停留點；完工後把變更寫入結構紀錄、竣工圖與模型，作為交接給物業管理與未來改造團隊的正式文件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Structural demolition in an occupied tower requires step-by-step construction-stage analysis and a temporary bracing plan, with every cut treated as a hold point; afterwards record the change in the structural log, as-built drawings and model as the formal handover to facility management and future renovation teams.","failure":"注意干擾：若先切除裙梁再補臨時支撐，柱在短時間內處於較長的無側撐狀態，遇到強風或施工荷載可能側向挫屈；改造後若竣工圖未更新，下一次改造的團隊會以錯誤的傳力路徑做評估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cutting the spandrel before installing temporary bracing leaves the column unbraced over a longer length for a while, and strong wind or construction loads could buckle it; if as-built drawings are not updated afterward, the next renovation team will assess an incorrect load path. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"拆除前以三維模型檢核每個拆除步驟的柱與相鄰構件需求容量比，臨時支撐安裝並驗收後才可切割；施工期間量測相鄰柱應變與垂直度，新裙梁接合完成並檢驗後才拆除臨時支撐，最後更新竣工圖與結構模型。","textEn":"Before demolition, check demand-to-capacity ratios of columns and adjacent members for every removal step in the three-dimensional model, and cut only after temporary bracing is installed and accepted; during the work monitor strain and plumbness of adjacent columns, remove temporary bracing only after the new spandrel connections are completed and inspected, then update the as-built drawings and structural model.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"營運中大樓的結構拆除必須有逐步的施工階段分析與臨時支撐計畫，切割作業列為停留點；完工後把變更寫入結構紀錄、竣工圖與模型，作為交接給物業管理與未來改造團隊的正式文件。","textEn":"Structural demolition in an occupied tower requires step-by-step construction-stage analysis and a temporary bracing plan, with every cut treated as a hold point; afterwards record the change in the structural log, as-built drawings and model as the formal handover to facility management and future renovation teams.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tube load path and records during alteration\"?","options":["拆除前以三維模型檢核每個拆除步驟的柱與相鄰構件需求容量比，臨時支撐安裝並驗收後才可切割。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","規範的近似週期公式可以準確預測超高層的實際振動週期。"],"optionsEn":["Before demolition, check demand-to-capacity ratios of columns and adjacent members for every removal step in the three-dimensional model, and cut only after temporary bracing is installed and accepted.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Code approximate-period formulas accurately predict the real period of a supertall tower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"拆除前以三維模型檢核每個拆除步驟的柱與相鄰構件需求容量比，臨時支撐安裝並驗收後才可切割；施工期間量測相鄰柱應變與垂直度，新裙梁接合完成並檢驗後才拆除臨時支撐，最後更新竣工圖與結構模型。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before demolition, check demand-to-capacity ratios of columns and adjacent members for every removal step in the three-dimensional model, and cut only after temporary bracing is installed and accepted; during the work monitor strain and plumbness of adjacent columns, remove temporary bracing only after the new spandrel connections are completed and inspected, then update the as-built drawings and structural model. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b028-v13-40","title":"改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tube load path and records during alteration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"prerequisiteIds":["b028-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口裙梁更換與柱無側撐長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Entrance spandrel replacement and column bracing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若先切除裙梁再補臨時支撐，柱在短時間內處於較長的無側撐狀態，遇到強風或施工荷載可能側向挫屈；改造後若竣工圖未更新，下一次改造的團隊會以錯誤的傳力路徑做評估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cutting the spandrel before installing temporary bracing leaves the column unbraced over a longer length for a while, and strong wind or construction loads could buckle it; if as-built drawings are not updated afterward, the next renovation team will assess an incorrect load path. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：裙梁不只抵抗側力，也為柱提供側向支撐；拆除後柱的無側撐長度變長，受壓挫屈強度隨之下降，必須在替換完成前以臨時支撐補足。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Spandrels do not only resist lateral load; they also brace the columns, so removing them lengthens the unbraced length and reduces buckling strength, which must be made up with temporary bracing until replacement is complete.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裙梁只是外牆的支承梁，拆除後不影響柱的承載力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Spandrels only support the façade, so removing one does not affect column capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b028-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若先切除裙梁再補臨時支撐，柱在短時間內處於較長的無側撐狀態，遇到強風或施工荷載可能側向挫屈；改造後若竣工圖未更新，下一次改造的團隊會以錯誤的傳力路徑做評估。","textEn":"Cutting the spandrel before installing temporary bracing leaves the column unbraced over a longer length for a while, and strong wind or construction loads could buckle it; if as-built drawings are not updated afterward, the next renovation team will assess an incorrect load path.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]},{"id":"b028-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「改造中的管筒傳力路徑與交接紀錄」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tube load path and records during alteration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若先切除裙梁再補臨時支撐，柱在短時間內處於較長的無側撐狀態，遇到強風或施工荷載可能側向挫屈；改造後若竣工圖未更新，下一次改造的團隊會以錯誤的傳力路徑做評估。","框管結構所有周邊柱都均勻分擔傾覆力矩產生的軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Cutting the spandrel before installing temporary bracing leaves the column unbraced over a longer length for a while, and strong wind or construction loads could buckle it.","All perimeter columns of a framed tube share the overturning axial force equally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若先切除裙梁再補臨時支撐，柱在短時間內處於較長的無側撐狀態，遇到強風或施工荷載可能側向挫屈；改造後若竣工圖未更新，下一次改造的團隊會以錯誤的傳力路徑做評估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cutting the spandrel before installing temporary bracing leaves the column unbraced over a longer length for a while, and strong wind or construction loads could buckle it; if as-built drawings are not updated afterward, the next renovation team will assess an incorrect load path. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-willis-tower","v13s-som-willis-tower","v13s-aisc-willis-50","v13s-aisc-ej-sears-floor","v13s-tt-willis-repositioning"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
